Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
This notebook contains code to build flashers with (mostly) uniformly thick \
panels that stack vertically in the stowed state. There are also functions \
for 3D-printing stowed versions with integral hinges (assuming a flexible \
3D-printing medium).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.913538574692025*^9, 3.913538651842848*^9}, 
   3.922122640871813*^9, {3.9226981266701927`*^9, 
   3.92269812718716*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4165d6c3-3e3a-4d53-b2fe-\
a5975875e5df"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook builds on the Tessellatica 14.x package, which is the first \
section of this notebook. Select and execute all of the cells in the first \
section of this notebook.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9135386574214582`*^9, 3.91353872476523*^9}, {
  3.913993517437995*^9, 3.913993522433403*^9}, {3.9843977248133583`*^9, 
  3.9843977536846323`*^9}, {3.984397788877934*^9, 
  3.984397796194191*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3b2aceb2-c3ab-4dcf-924b-\
83d83b0ad5da"],

Cell["\<\
After that, select and execute all cells in the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Thick \
Flashers\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section of the notebook, which will both \
load functions and run the various examples scattered through the notebook.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.913538726768955*^9, 3.913538753612329*^9}, {
  3.984397763331094*^9, 3.9843977652156563`*^9}, {3.98439780131032*^9, 
  3.9843978045412283`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9e9ffb44-c318-4365-967b-\
88068a46e063"],

Cell["\<\
The \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Figures\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section recreates \
all of the algorithmically generated figures on the paper.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.984397809914899*^9, 
  3.9843978294660797`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"085a0909-406a-48b9-8931-\
6b7a8042d7c7"],

