Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Importing 2D graphics in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " 8\[Dash]11"
}], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534428914750901*^9, 3.5344289224121847`*^9}, {
  3.589465723604349*^9, 3.589465724144994*^9}, {3.59204166476987*^9, 
  3.592041665200227*^9}, {3.675962848052373*^9, 3.675962851154428*^9}, {
  3.675963057023548*^9, 3.675963058088645*^9}, {3.7080148981636977`*^9, 
  3.708014898336681*^9}, {3.7202982139518633`*^9, 
  3.720298214639385*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"159165fc-0206-464e-a70a-\
9810142ce355"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534428930339737*^9, 
  3.534428930779532*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8ea7ac77-e4c1-4ff1-a093-\
c1ed07e171c2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Back in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " 7 and earlier, if you imported a line art drawing (like a crease pattern) \
from a PDF, it came in as a collection of Line objects (wrapped in Style \
directives, beginning with ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " 7). Starting in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " 8, it comes in as a collection of JoinedCurve objects, which take an \
undocumented (grumble) 3-argument form. This set of rules converts at least \
some of them to Lines[]. Typical usage is, Import the drawing, then apply \
this set of rules. You should check the visual appearance of the drawing pre- \
and post- application, to make sure it still looks right."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534428933203617*^9, 3.534428950226482*^9}, {
  3.534428981223982*^9, 3.534429141389683*^9}, {3.534429306210579*^9, 
  3.534429368574662*^9}, {3.589465524782465*^9, 
  3.5894655262576647`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d57f94ec-a8c1-46f9-bae7-\
e53d86901be1"],

Cell["\<\
Note that closed polygons will drop points and curves will get coarsely \
quantized (because they lose their control points). That\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
because the only things we\[CloseCurlyQuote]re importing are open patterns \
composed of straight-line segments.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.589465659950735*^9, 3.58946572031161*^9}, {
  3.592041710328093*^9, 
  3.592041722268137*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cd646b62-80b8-4f52-8c0b-\
e69caad707c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " 9\[Dash]11 can use the same rules as 8."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.675962910752222*^9, 3.675962921574314*^9}, {
  3.675963014658029*^9, 3.6759630187838373`*^9}, {3.675963066033154*^9, 
  3.6759630675335197`*^9}, {3.721630809937681*^9, 
  3.721630811483693*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b70c46ff-3426-4fa4-a305-\
a23f1f753f06"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

