Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tessellatica objects", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591376298982662*^9, 3.591376315827651*^9}, {
   3.5913804526582813`*^9, 3.591380455773965*^9}, 3.591637346449431*^9, 
   3.5916966112101603`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"90e882cd-b11e-4236-9d02-\
c04615358722"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5913785277159643`*^9, 
  3.591378529643352*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ff7530cb-f015-42c3-a4d7-\
8a56bcb51d01"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Once we start working with plane graphs and more complicated structures, we \
will be manipulating collections of data that we will refer to as a \
Tessellatica object, or TObj. The structure of a TObj is:\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"TObj", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["property",
         FontSlant->"Italic"], "1"], "\[Rule]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["value",
         FontSlant->"Italic"], "1"]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["property",
         FontSlant->"Italic"], "2"], "\[Rule]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["value",
         FontSlant->"Italic"], "2"]}], ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"3f9df4e0-4e77-4a38-932f-c17d20e15bcc"],
 "\nA TObj provides a way to encapsulate a bunch of related data in a single \
object. Instead of having to pass a bunch of lists to a function (like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["verts",
      FontSlant->"Italic"], ",", " ", 
     StyleBox["edges",
      FontSlant->"Italic"], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["faces",
       FontSlant->"Italic"], "..."}]}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"d6a52168-bb52-468d-a0ca-343f6d0d16fc"],
 "), you can pass a TObj that includes the properties Vertices, Edges, and \
Faces. We include functions for easy extraction of properties and also for \
error-checking to insure that required properties are present when passing a ",
 "TObj",
 " to a function."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591376318915106*^9, 3.591376488384912*^9}, {
  3.59137850672684*^9, 3.591378511572875*^9}, {3.591378743126358*^9, 
  3.591378781986843*^9}, {3.591637363619948*^9, 3.591637364600292*^9}, {
  3.591640209258236*^9, 3.591640213927642*^9}, {3.591640273047954*^9, 
  3.591640375901513*^9}, {3.5916963231715927`*^9, 3.591696564465053*^9}, {
  3.5924357286987143`*^9, 
  3.592435729318879*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ca1408cf-7dd8-4478-9de0-\
1f0ba15ac289"],

Cell["\<\
Functions can add data to the TObj by adding new properties and can alter \
TObj\[CloseCurlyQuote]s by changing existing properties. This section \
provides a set of functions for creating and working with TObj\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.591696386902013*^9, {3.591696573384556*^9, 3.591696589431928*^9}, {
   3.592346564445321*^9, 3.592346571650655*^9}, 3.59243572940849*^9, {
   3.593006306607237*^9, 
   3.593006312038776*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"02577632-04b9-4e16-b31a-\
0685986d1c28"]
}, Closed]],

