Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["TGraph merging and joining", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6435823650401173`*^9, 3.643582366008271*^9}, {
  3.6435824638902073`*^9, 3.643582469377097*^9}, {3.64994587368943*^9, 
  3.649945874961545*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cc94db14-5272-4bca-87ce-\
66b1e48d2bd7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.649945880609247*^9, 
  3.649945881041813*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"89f08144-8bdf-4a69-98a0-\
447e86efcff1"],

Cell["\<\
Often we\[CloseCurlyQuote]d like to combine multiple TGraphs in which some \
vertices overlap into a single TGraph. We do this via the related actions of 
\tMerging, where we simply combine the graphs at vertices that overlap, and 
\tJoining, in which we translate, scale, and/or rotate graphs so that \
multiple vertices are aligned before merging. 
In both cases, duplicated vertices and edges are either combined into one or \
entirely eliminated from the merged result, depending on option settings.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6499458836171703`*^9, 3.649945994441904*^9}, {
  3.649946224220705*^9, 3.649946226171479*^9}, {3.649947593811716*^9, 
  3.64994762159381*^9}, {3.649950822608362*^9, 3.649950866923715*^9}, {
  3.707763092328434*^9, 3.707763093494705*^9}, {3.707822185148666*^9, 
  3.70782220380478*^9}, {3.7078223367108717`*^9, 
  3.70782235153514*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"96e10964-ff50-41ae-ac11-\
c46fe8fa9ea0"],

Cell["\<\
See also similar functions in the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Crease-Assigned \
Graphs\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section, which do the same thing for graphs \
with defined fold types, fold angles, and 2D and 3D forms.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.649946024072141*^9, 3.649946073413356*^9}, {
  3.649946236202683*^9, 
  3.649946237506346*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"65a58a50-3a37-4234-b117-\
d185e3f398c7"],

Cell["\<\
You can also see the Joining concept used in the Tiling sections to implement \
the MonolithicTGraph, MonolithicTGraph2D, and MonolithicTGraph3D decorations.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.649946087540329*^9, 3.6499461039394007`*^9}, {
  3.707763525995308*^9, 
  3.70776355426709*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"efb29d46-8a74-4e09-a08b-\
51e1e4995774"],

Cell["\<\
We implement Merging via a 2-step process: first, generate a dataset via \
MergeGraphsData that specifies how the graphs should be merged; then use \
ApplyMergeData to actually construct the merged graph. We use this 2-step \
process so that we can expose the MergeGraphsData to functions that merge \
subclasses of TGraph. See, e.g., MergeGraphAssigneds, etc., to see how this \
is done.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707869308128733*^9, 3.707869477487767*^9}, {
  3.707905128623476*^9, 3.707905128689911*^9}, {3.707911514440804*^9, 
  3.70791151472529*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f76c9a9c-079e-499d-adcf-\
a981eaf38ccc"],

Cell["\<\
The Apply[*][To] routines are helpers that you should not call directly, \
unless you are building Merge and Join functions for more specialized \
subclasses.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707911412520086*^9, 
  3.707911497786965*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1bd47014-ad22-4b81-b233-\
68151b386483"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

