Cell[TextData[{
 "Graph2DGraphics[",
 StyleBox["tobj, opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] takes a TGraph+TGraph2D and displays vertices, edges, and faces with \
labels as a Graphics object using the alternate (Vertices2D) embedding. The \
faces, if present, are outlined with inset polygons. We change the color from \
the default GraphGraphics to emphasize the difference. Options are:\n\t\
Options[GenericGraphGraphics] are passed through to GenericGraphGraphics.\n\t\
Options[Graphics] are passed through to Graphics."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.455897664154768*^9, 3.455897679891059*^9}, {
   3.4558992977778797`*^9, 3.455899342784955*^9}, {3.455905103069544*^9, 
