Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3D folded forms", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592649376452248*^9, 3.5926493798157163`*^9}, {
   3.594687065710487*^9, 3.594687067004737*^9}, {3.687005555922722*^9, 
   3.687005557338587*^9}, {3.687006311931437*^9, 3.687006314026131*^9}, {
   3.6870063502557697`*^9, 3.687006350695856*^9}, 
   3.687461584351169*^9},ExpressionUUID->"8bf0121a-1d42-4193-8dbe-\
da914ec9a784"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5913658027005444`*^9, 
  3.591365803180267*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"84cd9f6f-93af-45fc-82b4-\
ffc9feff9217"],

Cell["\<\
We can represent a plane graph as a 3D surface by using 3D Vertices for the \
embedding. It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s obviously no longer a plane graph if its \
embedding is 3D, but we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll keep the terminology, calling it \
a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]3D plane graph.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Once we have \
a 3D embedding, we also can define fold angles for the edges that take on \
analog value between -\[Pi] (fully folded mountain fold) and +\[Pi] (fully \
folded valley fold). We introduce a new class, TGraph3D, and two new \
properties, Vertices3D and FoldAngles, to capture this information.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591365805972417*^9, 3.591365807603494*^9}, {
  3.591823826374599*^9, 3.591823827804633*^9}, {3.591958663884093*^9, 
  3.5919587100642543`*^9}, {3.591971611262394*^9, 3.5919716960734*^9}, {
  3.591972072449136*^9, 3.591972102774226*^9}, {3.5919726744972153`*^9, 
  3.591972675433071*^9}, {3.594725743082563*^9, 3.594725792886065*^9}, {
  3.594725836291591*^9, 
  3.594725860290411*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"54e33219-4c84-42d7-93fd-\
52780047ad3c"],

Cell["\<\
For objects whose folded form is 3D, a TGraph+TGraph3D can capture both the \
crease pattern (via Vertices) and the folded form (Vertices3D and \
FoldAngles), in the same way that a TGraph+TGraph2D captures both crease \
pattern (via Vertices) and folded form (via Vertices2D).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.594678478991398*^9, 3.594678512827575*^9}, {
  3.594725825085389*^9, 3.594725829067817*^9}, {3.594725864897916*^9, 
  3.594725886808001*^9}, {3.6152961865815287`*^9, 
  3.61529619572184*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7f872c54-af72-49bd-a50d-\
e0dc92f588b3"],

Cell["\<\
There is an implicit assumption in this section that the individual faces are \
planar in their 3D. If they\[CloseCurlyQuote]re not, then computed results \
will likely be invalid.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591978637013118*^9, 3.591978705721608*^9}, {
   3.591986933172607*^9, 3.591986933804476*^9}, {3.594229067789346*^9, 
   3.594229068554899*^9}, {3.594229284127261*^9, 3.594229301307585*^9}, 
   3.594725805101452*^9, {3.594725898047365*^9, 
   3.594725908322173*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8817e685-b3e2-4442-947e-\
ae9c27b5edce"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Class TGraph3D", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.533946193093484*^9, 3.533946200300918*^9}, {
   3.591823808447744*^9, 3.5918238122210913`*^9}, {3.591972108861928*^9, 
   3.591972120261344*^9}, {3.59240719176985*^9, 3.592407194022956*^9}, {
   3.592659627878694*^9, 3.5926596294615183`*^9}, 3.592828769625808*^9, {
   3.594685268688883*^9, 
   3.5946852696325893`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c7cb1f0-162d-4c65-8ff6-\
0da16685e2bd"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
TObj class: TGraph3D
\tMixin with: TGraph or subclass\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592467329567367*^9, 3.592467330811427*^9}, {
   3.592467362736558*^9, 3.592467383733872*^9}, {3.592467427882908*^9, 
   3.592467444672861*^9}, 
   3.5928287696767397`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"78e8507c-2dae-4065-81a5-\
c57261530413"],

Cell["\<\
TGraph3D is a mixin class that can be used to make any TGraph (or subclass of \
a a TGraph) a 3D embedded graph.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5923772061400437`*^9, 3.592377241344017*^9}, {
   3.592435857247558*^9, 3.592435857335558*^9}, 
   3.592828769730956*^9},ExpressionUUID->"06ddc2e6-e26a-46c7-8d3a-\
c7d82a5d06c9"],

Cell["\<\
Note that it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s possible for a TObj to inherit from both \
TGraph2D and TGraph3D. This can be useful for using the 3D embedding to \
represent the partially-folded state and the 2D embedding to represent the \
fully-folded state. (The original TGraph embedding represents the unfolded \
state.)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.615297693380075*^9, 3.615297702448881*^9}, {
  3.61529782758659*^9, 
  3.615297903598349*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a9671b80-74c9-4138-b230-\
46f372607fb8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TGraph3D", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<TGraph3D is a TObj class that describes a graph with a 3D \
embedding.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592377247205011*^9, 3.592377270456624*^9}, 
   3.592435744410511*^9, {3.592828769752657*^9, 3.5928287697843924`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1403]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1538242c-7520-4884-a711-c33aeb4536fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"RegisterTClass", "[", 
   RowBox[{"TGraph3D", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", "TGraph", "}"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5925190851323442`*^9, 3.59251908921311*^9}, {
   3.592519273305931*^9, 3.592519280007385*^9}, {3.592519331781473*^9, 
   3.592519333298522*^9}, 3.592641791168742*^9, 3.5928287698345757`*^9, {
   3.615297674933724*^9, 3.615297677356129*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1404]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3582183e-d1c4-4872-8c7f-6cc6d342be30"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
TGraph3D properties:
\tVertices3D
\tFoldAngles\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.59237710835288*^9, 3.592377121615912*^9}, 
   3.59243574416375*^9, 3.5926488742773843`*^9, 3.592828769891419*^9, {
   3.594229083009926*^9, 3.594229096042363*^9}, {3.5950090772597713`*^9, 
   3.595009077938769*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b6041541-7e96-495f-888d-\
a78d17919747"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices3D is a property that gives the 3D embedding of the vertices of a \
TGraph.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592377169132615*^9, 3.592377185243945*^9}, 
   3.592435857152151*^9, {3.594229177740074*^9, 
   3.594229180131421*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"116a1de2-493c-4541-b105-\
ab4c584930ab"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Vertices3D", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<Vertices3D is a TObj property that specifies a 3D embedding of \
the vertices of a graph.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.59237727961279*^9, 3.592377307622538*^9}, 
   3.592435744246968*^9, 3.594229125361625*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1405]:=",ExpressionUUID->"89cc5af3-6664-489e-baf7-349e7dd1bd91"],

Cell["\<\
FoldAngles is a list of the fold angles for each edge of the TGraph3D. By \
convention, border edges are assigned a fold angle of 0.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.594229140021976*^9, 
  3.594229167308494*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b0381054-b250-44dd-8395-\
e01b4eb1a1c0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FoldAngles", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<FoldAngles is a TObj property that specifies the angles of the \
folds for each edge of a TGraph3D.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.594229090948944*^9, 3.594229121596766*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1406]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a5234088-ac9c-41da-b0d0-fa8f03769ad4"]
}, Closed]],

