Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Primal-dual graphs", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592649396758642*^9, 
  3.5926493990301647`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"884d87ec-4bfd-48c7-abfb-\
cbb6b2999bab"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Class TPrimalDualGraph", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.466090367861568*^9, 3.466090379787118*^9}, {
   3.466095535451222*^9, 3.4660955449136477`*^9}, {3.592220789838613*^9, 
   3.592220793230411*^9}, {3.592240271096446*^9, 3.592240275829275*^9}, {
   3.592240312349246*^9, 3.592240322202068*^9}, {3.59240093399264*^9, 
   3.592400937199115*^9}, {3.592407198774867*^9, 3.592407201478571*^9}, {
   3.592659819387211*^9, 3.592659820906904*^9}, 3.5928288025280027`*^9, {
   3.5946853491815033`*^9, 
   3.594685349811669*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c44cb6e6-74f2-47fa-a9d1-\
fdf960bfd122"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591731572474948*^9, 
  3.591731572968932*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0ee1dfcf-1777-43a1-a16a-\
25fcb5515818"],

Cell["\<\
Many origami tessellation algorithms are based on a primal plane graph \
(representing vertices) and its dual graph (representing faces). In this \
section, we introduce a new TObj class, TPrimalDualGraph, and its properties \
(see below) so that a single TObj can contain information about both a primal \
graph and its dual in the same object.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591731574745694*^9, 3.591731676857105*^9}, {
   3.5924011763776817`*^9, 3.592401186094695*^9}, {3.592435745991966*^9, 
   3.592435746097114*^9}, 
   3.5928288026298037`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"bae73241-2b36-4fa3-8b2e-\
4d91db9f3ae1"],

Cell["\<\
We also introduce the notion of DualVertices, which are embeddings of \
vertices corresponding to the faces of the primal graph, and DualEdges, which \
are edges of the dual graph. There is the issue of how to handle the exterior \
of the graph -- is it a face? (Classical graph theory says yes), and then \
dual edges would extend across the boundary edges to this face. In our \
system, we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t include the exterior face as a face, and \
where we need to refer to it, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll give it the fictitious \
index of 0.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591789091543766*^9, 3.591789254229184*^9}, {
  3.592401202893429*^9, 3.592401227011031*^9}, {3.594303897284709*^9, 
  3.594303903544838*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f778f1d9-8aeb-46de-86fe-\
5fc5da5613a6"],

Cell["\<\
Since the dual graph we are interested in does not include the exterior as a \
face, it also does not include dual edges across the boundary of the graph. \
Our graph is thus the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]interior dual\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] graph, rather than the full dual. We also introduce \
the concept of InteriorEdges, which are those edges that are not on the \
boundary.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.59178926333582*^9, 3.591789325643946*^9}, {
  3.5922398524848843`*^9, 3.592239855193399*^9}, {3.59430391681564*^9, 
  3.594303939493901*^9}, {3.594303988363133*^9, 
  3.594304007881916*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"07effec4-3e85-4f97-a7f8-\
612fc85af83e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Primal-dual tessellations start with a plane graph, then construct the \
reciprocal diagram and use the two to create a tessellation for an arbitrary \
crease pattern. They include two types: twist tessellations (as in Alex \
Bateman\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox["Tess",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " program) and generalized flagstone tessellations. Both involve shrinking \
polygons of the primal graph about the vertices of the dual graph and are \
described further in the sections below."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.461743225891289*^9, 3.461743268630561*^9}, {
  3.461745129162431*^9, 3.461745129288905*^9}, {3.484834755214506*^9, 
  3.484834758843008*^9}, {3.484834798848946*^9, 3.484834799441287*^9}, {
  3.533591842918716*^9, 3.533591845765946*^9}, {3.551746319350251*^9, 
  3.551746356497162*^9}, {3.551746395646889*^9, 3.55174641198172*^9}, {
  3.551746558540364*^9, 3.551746559276637*^9}, {3.55174659129837*^9, 
  3.5517465985851393`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c030a162-4798-4a6d-86d7-\
d679c954237b"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
TObj class: TPrimalDualGraph
\tInherits from: TPlaneGraph\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592395099981977*^9, 3.592395106373265*^9}, 
   3.592435747017384*^9, {3.592435973897799*^9, 3.592435974707323*^9}, {
   3.592467556393777*^9, 3.592467561081461*^9}, 3.592828720741796*^9, 
   3.592828802685985*^9},ExpressionUUID->"b55939d0-666d-47f3-86ce-\
f0b12fe41291"],

Cell["\<\
TPrimalDualGraph is a TObj object that represents a primal graph together \
with a dual graph whose faces correspond to the vertices of the primal graph \
and vice-versa. A TPrimalDualGraph is descended from a TPlaneGraph.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5923951110378013`*^9, 3.592395146922494*^9}, {
   3.592401933838404*^9, 3.592401947675008*^9}, 3.592435747125572*^9, 
   3.59282872085785*^9, {3.592828802766762*^9, 
   3.592828802834675*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"00183f5b-9bad-42f7-9f3f-\
a1896887f94b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TPrimalDualGraph", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<TPrimalDualGraph is a TObj class that represents a primal graph \
together with its dual graph.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592401459479344*^9, 3.592401491037897*^9}, 
   3.592435747197517*^9, {3.592828802885943*^9, 3.592828802917844*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1475]:=",ExpressionUUID->"15b2e945-8adf-414b-bad9-53cf650d7775"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"RegisterTClass", "[", 
   RowBox[{"TPrimalDualGraph", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", "TPlaneGraph", "}"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5925190851323442`*^9, 3.59251908921311*^9}, {
   3.592519273305931*^9, 3.592519280007385*^9}, {3.592519384466976*^9, 
   3.592519390568194*^9}, 3.592641791218931*^9, 3.592828720954054*^9, 
   3.592828802969669*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1476]:=",ExpressionUUID->"195c6f19-a793-418b-8e0b-99c38fd7273a"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
TPrimalDualGraph properties:
\tDualVertices
\tInteriorEdges
\tDualEdges
\tDualFaces\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591737286650201*^9, 3.591737287869158*^9}, {
   3.592075552332304*^9, 3.5920755549311867`*^9}, {3.5922402490015717`*^9, 
   3.592240249600581*^9}, {3.592401329495523*^9, 3.592401353862162*^9}, {
   3.592436046290745*^9, 3.5924360470347233`*^9}, 3.592649466850629*^9, 
   3.592828803049912*^9, 3.594303398211512*^9, {3.594303465078805*^9, 
   3.594303506508218*^9}, {3.5950090956505327`*^9, 
   3.59500909785736*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"57c11395-3e73-4f23-84f7-\
47a08a5d0984"],

Cell["\<\
Of the lists below, only DualVertices contain coordinate values; all other \
data values are lists of indices.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.4660940372950377`*^9, 3.4660941016265182`*^9}, {
   3.592223904940653*^9, 3.592223913753682*^9}, {3.592223963910494*^9, 
   3.592223966285828*^9}, {3.5922243707183447`*^9, 3.5922243964256783`*^9}, 
   3.592401443390888*^9, {3.593212300133675*^9, 3.593212302574155*^9}, {
   3.594303423921347*^9, 
   3.594303426223789*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ac15e77a-6ccf-4a0b-af02-\
36910322133c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"DualVertices", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["v", "1"], ",", " ", 
      SubscriptBox["v", "2"], ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"cfa0e3f5-1db5-4a25-bf8a-efb34565bab2"],
 " is a ",
 "TObj",
 " property that specifies a list of dual graph vertices where each of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["v", "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8f3e2eec-b928-428b-b733-428c81170cee"],
 " is a 2D vertex coordinate set."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591731686201055*^9, 3.591731753600017*^9}, 
   3.5920707885412807`*^9, 
   3.592435746181394*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4f7f8c75-b7fe-4a67-8e97-\
a41c373af06b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"DualVertices", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<DualVertices is a TObj property specifying vertices of a dual \
graph as a list of vertex coordinates.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.59164547165294*^9, 3.591645529238023*^9}, 
   3.59172174863381*^9, 3.592075630784754*^9, 3.5924357462630157`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1477]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7324a3fa-a421-417f-a1b4-af5885403211"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"DualEdges", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["f", "i"], ",", " ", 
        SubscriptBox["f", "j"]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"889ddd85-a93a-4882-9f5d-f763dbdcb4cb"],
 " is a TObj property specifying a list of dual graph edges as index pairs on \
the faces of the primary graph (vertices of the dual graph)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591731760183196*^9, 3.591731886318893*^9}, {
   3.592240370768002*^9, 3.5922404176278253`*^9}, 3.5924357463535557`*^9, {
   3.593212305110024*^9, 
   3.5932123093815517`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e52feb5c-07be-40a3-a10e-\
3e6990060153"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"DualEdges", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<DualEdges is a TObj property specifying edges of a dual graph as \
a list of index pairs into DualVertices.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.591721752595155*^9, 3.59207563079515*^9, {3.592401581936128*^9, 
   3.5924015887178087`*^9}, 3.592435746428735*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1478]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4a4e01b4-39a7-4387-a81d-9616a07706e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"DualFaces", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["f", "i"], ",", " ", 
        SubscriptBox["f", "j"], ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], ",", " ", "..."}], 
     "}"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "aac37c31-c42b-42b0-a4ce-822ee72b408d"],
 " is a ",
 "TObj",
 " property that specifies the dual graph faces around each of the \
InteriorVertices as lists of indices into DualVertices. This also gives the \
cyclic order of the faces around each interior vertex."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592237244481174*^9, 3.592237338929714*^9}, 
   3.5922378158750753`*^9, {3.592237885314389*^9, 3.592237961109007*^9}, 
   3.5924357465235786`*^9, {3.593212340636991*^9, 
   3.593212361161931*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c047ef45-ce73-4cd8-928c-\
3284c82c0439"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"DualFaces", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<DualFaces is a TObj property that specifies the dual graph faces \
as lists of indices into DualVertices.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.592232578946563*^9, 3.592232610139496*^9}, {
   3.59223265074053*^9, 3.592232657288866*^9}, {3.592237145081678*^9, 
   3.592237180751466*^9}, 3.5924357465996513`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1479]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d1639673-2cef-4b16-9590-443667e91d4e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"InteriorEdges", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["v", "i"], ",", " ", 
        SubscriptBox["v", "j"]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"7f5ae7a9-dcf0-4aa4-88da-6221fd55abda"],
 " is a key to a TObj that specifies the interior edge pairs of a plane \
graph, i.e., those not on the boundary, as ordered pairs of vertex indices. \
They may be ordered differently from the ordered pairs in Edges, because \
InteriorEdges and DualEdges (also ordered pairs of indices) have a defined \
relative ordering: the direction of a dual edge pair is a CCW rotation \
relative to the direction of its corresponding interior edge pair."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591737295549032*^9, 3.591737429701787*^9}, {
   3.592237461773553*^9, 3.592237462226181*^9}, {3.592239943961933*^9, 
   3.592239986113295*^9}, {3.5922401016345167`*^9, 3.5922402159572883`*^9}, 
   3.592435746857469*^9, {3.5943034508390417`*^9, 3.594303451677887*^9}, {
   3.594304036112928*^9, 
   3.59430410538739*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"47dd2300-4cb1-40eb-8515-\
13ec1c5ec493"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"InteriorEdges", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<InteriorEdges is a TObj property that specifies the interior \
edges of a plane graph as ordered pairs of vertex indices.\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.59173739522702*^9, 3.591737416684911*^9}, 
   3.592070788628408*^9, {3.592240226163873*^9, 3.592240231899435*^9}, 
   3.592435746932199*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1480]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7ad9bf33-1593-41ce-884b-daf72bae96b6"]
}, Closed]],

