   3.707939484285768*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fbaaf479-feaf-405e-8a7e-\
72371a620771"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "FacesAboveOld[",
 StyleBox["tobj",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] takes a list ",
 StyleBox["dedges",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of directed edges on the faces of a crease pattern that defines a local \
ordering graph on the faces and returns a list where the ",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "th entry in the list is a list of the indices of all the faces that lie \
above the ith face."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.484786448732294*^9, 3.484786498312599*^9}, {
   3.484786583459317*^9, 3.484786680572295*^9}, 3.484786789373294*^9, {
   3.484787466178838*^9, 3.484787502624229*^9}, 3.484788888008327*^9, {
   3.594735127833872*^9, 3.594735129449106*^9}, 3.628786944512294*^9, {
   3.6288661765887823`*^9, 3.6288661847178717`*^9}, 3.628869570935441*^9, 
   3.628889153355448*^9, {3.628890620198003*^9, 
   3.628890620908574*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3dc16b02-e674-4fec-92dd-\
dbf917960696"],

Cell["\<\
As its (new) name suggests, it is deprecated. We have a new and improved \
algorithm below.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.628891085343117*^9, 
  3.628891099974273*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bfd58a10-a7e0-4442-b6c3-\
738c62724c4d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This uses a heuristic algorithm: it simply returns every face within \
MaxDistance above the ",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "th face. To get all faces above each face, pass the value \
MaxDistance\[Rule]\[Infinity]."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.628866187520183*^9, 
  3.628866214616868*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7a5e3672-998e-40c4-ae4e-\
597962c11310"],

Cell["\<\
Note, however, that with cyclic twists, every facet in a cycle lies \"above\" \
any one of the facets. The way we break the cycle, which is somewhat \
heuristic, is that we look for cycles (pairs in the all-pairs-shortest-path \
matrix that are symmetric about the diagonal) and we assume \"shortest path \
wins\"; that is, the shortest path in the cycle describes the proper ordering \
relationship between the two facets. In case of a tie, we'll assume \
incomparability.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.486164911647396*^9, 3.486164916973092*^9}, {
  3.486165055393918*^9, 3.48616505975561*^9}, {3.486165110072593*^9, 
  3.486165218712846*^9}, {3.486165314210793*^9, 3.4861653178671083`*^9}, {
  3.486165393598181*^9, 3.486165416651979*^9}, {3.486165493760567*^9, 
  3.486165575097601*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"46f735ad-a788-4aca-8b65-\
6a2f1da08228"],

Cell["\<\
This is a simple heuristic that does surprisingly well for rendering a \
plausible folded form. We note, though, something as simple as a VVMVM \
pentagonal twist tile defeats it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591805446237715*^9, 3.591805495032837*^9}, {
  3.628891128292544*^9, 
  3.628891138227132*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1659a44e-8b79-4089-93d2-\
915d806c3660"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MaxDistance", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<MaxDistance is an option to FacesAboveOld that specifies how far \
away we look for a covering-up face.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591805542354648*^9, 3.591805573203074*^9}, 
   3.628786944533853*^9, 3.62886957096418*^9, 3.628889160377671*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1876]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9613edbb-51e6-49d6-b535-f390838945e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Options", "[", "FacesAboveOld", "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"MaxDistance", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"ShowProgress", "\[Rule]", "False"}], ","}], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.48478650926908*^9, 3.4847865732780943`*^9}, 
   3.484788888029619*^9, 3.48482056594088*^9, 3.628786944542341*^9, 
   3.628869571219545*^9, 3.6288891552642508`*^9, {3.6288892356802397`*^9, 
   3.62888924045429*^9}},
 CellLabel->
