   3.62896737831083*^9}, 
   3.7079233317904873`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a69b6c66-fd65-4fe3-afad-\
a815f8bae4d1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Options:\n\tFacesAbove \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["fa",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " | Automatic, where ",
 StyleBox["fa",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a list of of the face indices that lie above each face. Automatic means \
we calculate it using our own algorithm, which will make use of FaceupFace, \
see next.\n\tFaceupFace \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["fuface",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " specifies a face-up face if we have to calculate our own facet ordering.\n\
\tShowProgress \[Rule] True | False, if true, display some graphs showing the \
relationships that are used along the way.\n\tReportInconsistentOrdering \
\[Rule] True | False, if true, post a Message if an inconsistent ordering was \
detected; passed through to FacesAboveAutomatic (if used).\n\t\
Options[Graphics] are passed through."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7079233339026*^9, 3.707923336940654*^9}, 
   3.707923427727206*^9, {3.7079235012158747`*^9, 
   3.707923523286996*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d2978eba-1ac6-409b-a406-\
452ad0f66deb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FacesAbove", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<FacesAbove is an option to VisibleFoldedFormLines that specifies \
whether to calculate facet ordering from local ordering or to provide an \
explicit list of indices of faces lying about each face.\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.591805794802464*^9, 3.591805857011589*^9}, 
   3.592179948331502*^9, 3.592208038557734*^9, 3.592433623497407*^9, 
