Cell[TextData[{
 "CreasePatternToPlaneGraphAssigned[",
 StyleBox["cp, opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] takes a list of Line segments styled with some combination of the four \
crease pattern line types: MountainLine, ValleyLine, ",
 "UnfoldedLine",
 ", BorderLine) and extracts and returns a crease-assigned plane graph \
description, TPlaneGraphAssigned. Note that if BorderOverride \[Rule] True, \
whatever line style you assigned to the border lines, they will be given edge \
type B. Options are:\n\tSamePtTolerance \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["tol",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", where ",
 StyleBox["tol",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is the tolerance on distance used when the vertices are Indexified.\n\t\
BorderOverride \[Rule] True | False, where True overrides whatever you've set \
the border lines to and sets them to edge type B."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.48486435792052*^9, 3.4848644230603*^9}, {
   3.484864457147197*^9, 3.484864482904033*^9}, {3.484864522358801*^9, 
