Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534542991574278*^9, 
  3.534542991990301*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d616813d-8ba6-429d-9585-\
92378678e99d"],

Cell["\<\
Kawasaki identified problems with local flat-foldability that could arise \
from the interaction of multiple vertices, by identifying what he called \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Type I\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Type II\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] vertices in d4v \
networks; if a closed cycle contains an odd number of the wrong type of \
angles, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s not locally flat foldable. To easily identify \
such situations, we introduce a plane graph, the LFF graph (LFF = \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]local flat-foldability\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]), which \
is a graph drawn on the interior edges of the crease pattern.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.534542993934965*^9, 3.534543162331065*^9}, {
  3.594740828497652*^9, 
  3.594740846319394*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d3314d97-e1ac-4a36-9e28-\
81051dc7ac25"]
}, Closed]],

