Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Crease-assigned meshes", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5940591399084244`*^9, 3.5940591424586487`*^9}, 
   3.594060017227308*^9, {3.6173056247536783`*^9, 3.617305625519596*^9}, {
   3.617444146640888*^9, 3.617444148540023*^9}, {3.64338809287038*^9, 
   3.643388094446957*^9}, 3.693415414584266*^9, {3.701173809668356*^9, 
   3.701173810277758*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"30633459-75b6-43b7-b4d1-\
1be791a51fec"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.594061148221299*^9, 
  3.594061148649863*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4f527aab-0d33-4ef1-81c6-\
07bfcd764ab7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A quadrilateral mesh is a mesh in which the vertices can be indexed on two \
indices ",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["j",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", with the numbering in a rectangular array: ",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[Element] [0, ",
 StyleBox["nh",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "], ",
 StyleBox["j",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[Element] [0, ",
 StyleBox["nv",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.69341610376423*^9, 
  3.693416182100932*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7a5bab3d-1a08-4cc6-8676-\
b0490b671480"],

Cell["\<\
The functions in this section construct quadrilateral meshes based on \
user-supplied functions for coordinate values and, optionally, edge types. \
They are useful for generating crease patterns directly (e.g., Miura-ori), \
and for generating graphs used in primal-dual tessellations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5940611504861526`*^9, 3.594061208549843*^9}, {
  3.5940703840941963`*^9, 3.594070385531126*^9}, {3.642607499198262*^9, 
  3.642607499733555*^9}, {3.693416230141086*^9, 
  3.693416236813388*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"74edb6c9-9f66-449a-9875-\
eb71e29eba07"],

Cell["\<\
We allow for the possibility of merging vertices; if two or more vertices \
have their defining coordinates at the same point, they can be merged into a \
single vertex. Thus, the actual facets of such a quad mesh could be \
triangles, rather than quadrilaterals. The \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]quad\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]-ness refers to the indexing scheme.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.642432725252582*^9, 3.6424327967105*^9}, {
  3.6426075161576037`*^9, 3.642607519967483*^9}, {3.693416254765307*^9, 
  3.6934162640534*^9}, {3.693416302686096*^9, 
  3.693416386318655*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f512fce8-a944-41f4-b32d-\
170aad431438"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Class TCornerIndices", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.457626126793686*^9, 3.457626137951227*^9}, 
   3.457748300260912*^9, {3.484780428903769*^9, 3.4847804299036427`*^9}, {
   3.533679695254013*^9, 3.5336796989817047`*^9}, {3.533680490818307*^9, 
   3.533680495088798*^9}, {3.533682700408101*^9, 3.533682700719997*^9}, {
   3.592421741611268*^9, 3.592421746856297*^9}, 3.592471907894451*^9, {
   3.592489932641145*^9, 3.592489934696615*^9}, {3.592490033361484*^9, 
   3.592490037377114*^9}, {3.592644843741893*^9, 3.5926448578114038`*^9}, {
   3.592660550278584*^9, 3.592660551315735*^9}, 3.5928288618952723`*^9, {
   3.594685354939475*^9, 3.594685355875361*^9}, 
   3.643238129507872*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4a909b32-e85e-4d80-b90e-\
b1bd4a0300bb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.457626158317848*^9, 
  3.457626158821782*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"61fc8c02-136c-4354-a12d-\
fa3956eaf45a"],

Cell["\<\
TCornerIndices is a mixin class that has the property CornerIndices, which \
specifies the indices of the corners of the mesh, i.e., the mesh can be \
considered to be some sort of generalized quadrilateral. \
It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s often useful for manipulating objects as crease \
patterns and folded forms.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.642610350268178*^9, 3.642610386735517*^9}, {
  3.643238022893188*^9, 3.643238110647987*^9}, {3.64324036707397*^9, 
  3.643240367456376*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1a1cdc26-228a-4ee8-ae36-\
3cc15cd7af53"],

Cell["\<\
One of the uses of TCornerIndices is it permits easy rotation of a 3D form so \
that three of the four original corners lie in the x-y plane, via this idiom:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.703606303964477*^9, 3.703606348012491*^9}, {
  3.703606491839949*^9, 
  3.703606494605906*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b517d84f-15fb-4aa7-8909-\
dded6a566cda"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"VertexRotateGraph3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tobj", ",", 
     RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
        RowBox[{"tobj", "[", "CornerIndices", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "3"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}], "//", "Hold"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.703606349698315*^9, 3.703606398637*^9}, 
   3.7036064870380993`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[2057]:=",ExpressionUUID->"78fc4461-e743-4680-aa98-3f019a57fae4"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
TObj class: TCornerIndices
\tMixin with: TGraph or any subclass\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5924679148960323`*^9, 3.592467936783182*^9}, 
   3.592486866349741*^9, {3.592486897902196*^9, 3.592486898475609*^9}, 
