   3.597672354626514*^9},ExpressionUUID->"adc5537a-54cc-4145-963b-\
23d5d4bf0b26"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Vertex3DGaussianSphereGraphics3D[",
 StyleBox["tobj",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] takes a TVertex3D and produces a graphical rendering of the vertex as a \
trace on the Gaussian sphere."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.594806497948852*^9, {3.594806627483521*^9, 3.594806649003462*^9}, 
   3.5948067448546677`*^9, {3.594806801712467*^9, 3.594806819207413*^9}, {
   3.5950203134103193`*^9, 3.595020341876587*^9}, {3.597525700243584*^9, 
   3.597525744367383*^9}, 3.5976723547530947`*^9, {3.703969083699424*^9, 
   3.703969090517305*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cc8856b3-d47a-4f5d-b8c6-\
63e0c17f1cdb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Options:\n\tShowGaussianSphere \[Rule] True | False, specifies whether to \
draw the bounding sphere of the Gaussian sphere.\n\tShowMidfoldVectors \
\[Rule] True | False, specifies whether to show the midarc vectors on the \
Gaussian sphere.\n\tGaussianSphereRadius \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["r",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", specifies the radius of the gaussian sphere (default is 0.99, so line \
arcs are barely outside the sphere).\n\tOptions[CircularAngleLabels] are \
passed through to specify dihedral and sector angle labels and position\n\t\
Options[Graphics3D] are passed through."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7039690925572042`*^9, 
  3.703969094667554*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b259a120-53e1-4a84-9353-\
dbfdeeab672f"],

