Cell["\<\
These examples are specific cases for a numerically defined vertex that we \
can use for checking our trigonometric identities. Each of the expressions \
should evaluate to zero when the identify is satisfied.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.594850453184664*^9, 3.59485045940808*^9}, {
  3.594850507604752*^9, 3.594850520893137*^9}, {3.594851084176968*^9, 
  3.59485110302488*^9}, {3.5948528101544333`*^9, 3.594852810448211*^9}, {
  3.594897388474606*^9, 3.594897397159577*^9}, {3.594898424021473*^9, 
  3.59489843310794*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3275ec80-7398-42f4-a789-\
aee93d7fc560"],

Cell["\<\
Throughout this section, a list of four sector angles is assumed (without \
checking) to be developable, i.e., summing to 2\[Pi].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6174339854338427`*^9, 3.617434007993083*^9}, {
  3.617436208555216*^9, 
  3.617436212826831*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"39f9bfae-a68b-4714-b31f-\
c340c3c41fd3"]
}, Closed]],

