   3.61743829275349*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fb2b15ec-3ffd-4a01-9fdc-\
4e98571d6714"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"MakeFoldVectorsFromSectorsAndMajorDihedral", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "1"], ",", " ", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "2"], ",", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "3"], ",", " ", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "4"]}], "}"}], ",", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", "1"], ",", 
     StyleBox["opts",
      FontSlant->"Italic"]}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0cd8895a-36bc-4334-972e-765b85bb4dfd"],
 " constructs a valid TDegree4Vertex3D from the sector angles and the \
specified major dihedral angle. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", "1"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fc0957d6-782f-4870-9bca-5f73a84aef19"],
 " is taken to run along the ",
 StyleBox["x",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " axis initially, although we then rotate to align the osculating vector if \
one is specified. Useful for constructing visual examples. Options are:\n\t\
Options[MakeDihedralsFromSectorsAndMinorDihedral] (AllowSelfIntersection) are \
passed through.\n\tOptions[MakeFoldVectorsFromSectorsAndDihedrals] \
(OsculatingVectorNear) are passed through."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.44044481625184*^9, 3.440444858689953*^9}, 
