Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "FoldLinearChain[",
 StyleBox["tobj",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", \[Gamma], ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]\n\t(options) RotateToZ"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.617379758802778*^9, 3.617379770132204*^9}, {
   3.617402645125525*^9, 3.6174026592011766`*^9}, 3.617402853261955*^9, {
   3.617403284509987*^9, 
   3.617403308999584*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f758977b-1beb-4436-bab1-\
e21abe860ca4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "FoldLinearChain[",
 StyleBox["tobj",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", \[Gamma]] takes a TLinearChain and (re)folds it into 3D (turning it into \
a TLinearChain+TGraph3D) by setting the first dihedral angle to \[Gamma]; \
this determines all of the other fold angles in the structure. Note that this \
will flip the type assignment of all creases if the first crease is changed \
from mountain to valley. Options are:\n\tRotateToZ \[Rule] True | False. If \
False, the first face (lower left) will be the stationary face, i.e., left in \
the x-y plane. If True, the structure will be rotated so that the V of a \
valley fold points in the +z direction (and the opposite for a mountain fold)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.617379777999917*^9, 3.617379840065694*^9}, {
  3.61738054844525*^9, 3.6173806093536863`*^9}, {3.617397022578576*^9, 
  3.617397082843616*^9}, {3.61740260000261*^9, 3.6174026215825243`*^9}, {
  3.61740266598208*^9, 3.6174026887992907`*^9}, {3.6174027247174053`*^9, 
  3.6174027393635178`*^9}, {3.617402866764976*^9, 3.617402903639597*^9}, {
  3.617403181340857*^9, 3.61740318393968*^9}, {3.617403289760296*^9, 
  3.617403383935259*^9}, {3.617440113993922*^9, 
  3.617440137409532*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"62cd9436-fde9-4c6f-a5ec-\
7438345125a6"],

Cell["\<\
Folding will fail and an error thrown if there are any straight-major \
vertices in the pattern. Also, if the initial crease would cause one of the \
other creases to go beyond the binding angle for that vertex, folding will \
also fail.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.617396608803927*^9, 3.617396620285265*^9}, {
  3.617397087987297*^9, 3.617397107727425*^9}, {3.617397154340462*^9, 
  3.617397196139231*^9}, {3.617404477540675*^9, 3.617404526944577*^9}, {
  3.617440159033358*^9, 
  3.617440162138956*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1ac4050d-9352-4c00-9154-\
7d77f82621f2"],

Cell["\<\
You should not set the fold angle to zero and then try to set it back to \
something nonzero, because the former will wipe out the crease assignment \
along the spine, which we use to determine the remaining assignments.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.617404480209079*^9, {3.617440170662589*^9, 
   3.61744019387172*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"53d95d0b-f44c-48d3-a707-\
b9d7b9f78506"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"RotateToZ", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<RotateToZ is an option to FoldLinearChain that specifies to \
rotate the folded form so that the first fold is oriented toward the +z \
direction.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.617403389628688*^9, 3.617403443504628*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[2418]:=",ExpressionUUID->"170745ed-e805-4587-be4d-5d7ee6e8fce0"],

