   3.594944615385063*^9},ExpressionUUID->"1f7c6ac5-c6e7-46a3-9d35-\
32d2416736a4"],

Cell["\<\
The construction of a dihedral angle that could follow an arbitrary 3D space \
curve is a problem that Ron Resch commented upon often in his talks, stating \
that he\[CloseCurlyQuote]d published a general solution (hinting that it was \
a differential geometric solution). I was never able to get him to give a \
specific reference for the algorithm, though. The solution below is discrete \
and, therefore, exact for a polyhedral curve.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.533657448254273*^9, 3.533657544318866*^9}, {
  3.594945383452207*^9, 
  3.594945385027773*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bac3a32f-1d2f-4d34-b7e1-\
8b3c845ff34c"],

Cell["\<\
Historically, I wrote this before writing class TLinearChain. TBD, rewrite \
this class so it inherits from TLinearChain.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.617405186029108*^9, 
  3.617405227116775*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1091b5f4-444f-4038-a628-\
d413ae4c77ea"]
}, Closed]],

