Cell["\<\
A Gauss map is a form of dual graph in which nodes of the graph are unit \
normal vectors to the faces of the primal graph and edges of the dual graph \
are arcs of great circles. We implement Gauss maps as a specialization of \
TPrimalDualGraph, by adding a 3D representation of the dual graph vertices.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.703966627333322*^9, 
  3.703966705358013*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6cb44f3a-9265-47c8-ad40-\
74b422d7b262"],

Cell["\<\
This is the same thing we show in Vertex3DGaussianSphereGraphics3D, but \
GaussMapGraphics3D returns the map for an entire folded form consisting of \
multiple vertices.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.703976159757338*^9, 
  3.703976244660617*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"32777940-3695-45a2-a56a-\
3201ddbac103"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "GaussMapGraphics3D[",
 StyleBox["tobj",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]\n\t(checked classes) TPrimalDualGraph, TGraph3D\n\t(checked properties) \
DualVertices3D\n\t(options) ShowGaussianSphere, GaussianSphereRadius, \
Options[Graphics3D]"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7039679244649076`*^9, 3.7039679329526987`*^9}, {
  3.703967982820205*^9, 3.703967992832736*^9}, {3.703968625951462*^9, 
  3.703968630999412*^9}, {3.8000023081747704`*^9, 
  3.800002345566554*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"288b56a4-44bd-44f5-b5c6-\
611a9ae8ddcc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "GaussMapGraphics3D[",
 StyleBox["tobj",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] creates a graphical representation of the Gauss map of a 3D surface \
represented by a TPrimalDualGraph+TGraph3D."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.703967936089361*^9, 3.703967965441419*^9}, {
  3.703976045469149*^9, 
  3.7039760561386356`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ce5ba840-c998-41db-9232-\
37b5b52aac5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Arguments:\n\t",
 StyleBox["tobj",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] a TPrimalDualGraph+TGraph3D."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7039680074733143`*^9, 3.703968047346212*^9}, 
   3.70397606125911*^9},ExpressionUUID->"1a4adb0c-0ae4-4d82-a630-\
e4d99285e9ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Options:\n\tShowGaussianSphere \[Rule] True | False, include a gray \
Gaussian sphere in the display.\n\tGaussianSphereRadius \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["r",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", specify the radius to use for the Gaussian sphere.\n\tOptions[Graphics3D] \
are passed through."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.703968050818184*^9, 3.703968091322544*^9}, {
  3.8000023503026037`*^9, 
  3.800002385934812*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bce40cf4-21c4-4999-ae51-\
9dc13f1b936c"],

Cell["Returns a Graphics3D object displaying the Gauss map.", "Text",
