Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tiling-based tessellations", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.533644991316751*^9, 3.533644993858878*^9}, 
   3.592170665508868*^9, 3.627385975402614*^9, {3.631187385187476*^9, 
   3.631187385841789*^9}, {3.70775511377479*^9, 
   3.707755114175297*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4b859520-a781-4112-b0dc-\
8bde02d4e486"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.457744215389313*^9, 3.457744215811485*^9}, 
   3.627385975403102*^9},ExpressionUUID->"679e57a9-862a-40b8-949c-\
0a9c737915ac"],

Cell["\<\
This section creates tiling-based tessellations, where we assemble individual \
tiles that obey various matching rules to create full-fledged origami \
tessellations: both crease patterns and representations of their folded form. \
The distinguishing concept here is, for a tiling-based tessellation, one \
develops crease patterns in tiles in such a way that when the tiles form a \
valid tessellation, the creases within the tiles form a valid crease pattern \
and/or folded form.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.485198356538093*^9, 3.485198361673794*^9}, 
   3.627385975403472*^9, {3.627652728434441*^9, 
   3.627652773504469*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1550e132-7b90-470b-8f0c-\
3b259e15b9e3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We create a tiling by a call to EmbedTiling[",
 StyleBox["tiling",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["decoration",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "], where ",
 StyleBox["tiling",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a list of ",
 StyleBox["tilespecs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", each of which describes an individual tile, including its type, shape, \
and family; ",
 StyleBox["decoration",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", which specifies one or more of several possible patterns that can be used \
to decorate each tile; and ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", which control optional modifications that are applied to the entire \
tiling."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.62976157385012*^9, 3.62976169745668*^9}, {
  3.629974301974482*^9, 3.629974339809108*^9}, {3.707772959273909*^9, 
  3.707772959656334*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6811a6e8-4585-4c0c-846a-\
fa2e19567851"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["tilespec",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a list {",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["offset",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["rotation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["scale",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "}, that specifies the size, position, and orientation of a tile ",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". So a ",
 StyleBox["tiling",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", a list of ",
 StyleBox["tilespecs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", is a set of multiple copies of (usually a small number of) ",
 StyleBox["tiletypes",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", specifying their size, position, and orientation."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.629761734418456*^9, 3.62976179911419*^9}, 
   3.629819849088315*^9, {3.629974376047035*^9, 
   3.629974446249636*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bbd6bf2a-84c9-4e82-9ea7-\
26d80b5d99bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, ",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a list {",
 StyleBox["tilename",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["parms",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "...}, that specifies a particular type of tile. The number of parameters ",
 StyleBox["parms",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is variable and depends on the ",
 StyleBox["tilename",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Examples of these are:\n\t{PolygonTile, ",
 StyleBox["verts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "} - represents an arbitrary polygon, specified by its vertices\n\t\
{UnitRegularPolygonTile, ",
 StyleBox["n",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "} \[LongDash] represents a unit regular ",
 StyleBox["n",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "-gon tile.\n\t{PolygonCenteredTwistTile, ",
 StyleBox["verts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["w",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", \[Tau], ",
 StyleBox["types",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "} \[LongDash] represents a centered twist tessellation tile.\n\t\
{UnitTrapezoidOffsetTwistTile, \[Delta], ",
 StyleBox["w",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["d",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["types",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "} \[LongDash] represents a unit trapezoid offset twist tessellation tile."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.629761804658101*^9, 3.6297618654384737`*^9}, {
  3.6297619164032297`*^9, 3.6297620846878653`*^9}, {3.629819864279849*^9, 
  3.629819864492411*^9}, {3.629974459815548*^9, 3.629974506469988*^9}, {
  3.6299745377238507`*^9, 
  3.62997453921193*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c69a4e4-ae90-45fd-84b4-\
115515d15194"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "By convention, the ",
 StyleBox["tilename",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for any ",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " will end in the word Tile, as above."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.629762416875201*^9, 3.629762434585327*^9}, {
  3.629974567778238*^9, 3.629974684842186*^9}, {3.707753477353915*^9, 
  3.707753478969168*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"66ccbb43-e79a-4085-ae74-\
07932c627438"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For any ",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", we define one or more forms of ",
 StyleBox["decoration",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that can be used to render the tile. In general, every ",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " should support the two decorations TileVertices and Tiling; the former is \
used to obtain positional information about the tiling, the second is used to \
render the tiling in its simplest form. The rest are optional. Possible \
decorations are as follows:\n\tTileVertices \[LongDash] every ",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " must support this, which is a list of the vertices of the tile polygon.\n\t\
Tiling \[LongDash] an abstract graphical representation of the tile, e.g., \
its outline, and optional arrows, colorings, and/or labels.\n\tCreasePattern \
\[LongDash] graphical elements that render the crease pattern of the tile.\n\t\
FoldedForm2D \[LongDash] graphical elements that render the 2D folded form of \
the tile.\n\tFoldedForm3D \[LongDash] graphical elements that render the 3D \
folded form of the tile.\n\tTGraphAssigned \[LongDash] a TGraphAssigned that \
represents the crease pattern of the tile.\n\tTGraph2DAssigned \[LongDash] a \
TGraph2DAssigned that represents the crease pattern and folded form of the \
tile.\n\tTGraph3DAssigned \[LongDash] a TGraph3DAssigned that represents the \
crease pattern and 3D folded form of the tile."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.62976211645424*^9, 3.629762348870897*^9}, {
   3.629819902226321*^9, 3.62981998767625*^9}, 3.62984750649771*^9, {
   3.62997471258521*^9, 3.629974794299739*^9}, {3.7077545387963977`*^9, 
   3.7077545449226*^9}, {3.707755194936303*^9, 3.707755214745206*^9}, {
   3.7077571744832983`*^9, 3.70775718749111*^9}, {3.707837689408458*^9, 
   3.707837709714823*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"210934ec-20a8-49eb-981a-\
3d0d04c421f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tiletypes and decorations are implemented by creating an implementation of \
the function RenderTile[",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["decoration",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] for all supported forms of ",
 StyleBox["decoration",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Remember that ",
 StyleBox["tiletype",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a list ",
 StyleBox["{tilename, parms}",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.629762499533585*^9, 3.629762555874271*^9}, {
  3.629762602743207*^9, 3.6297626136304812`*^9}, {3.629762656537614*^9, 
  3.62976267077083*^9}, {3.629820015242559*^9, 3.629820018067375*^9}, {
  3.707756147507606*^9, 
  3.707756159553312*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"02989803-ff6e-4ab3-8135-\
a776e8021266"],

Cell["\<\
A general-purpose tile should support decorations TileVertices and Tiling.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707757211346702*^9, 3.707757231194132*^9}, {
  3.707771087822678*^9, 
  3.707771091166585*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"35e1d8ef-381a-4806-a9dc-\
0b1963616371"],

Cell["\<\
In addition to those, an origami tessellation tile should support decorations \
TGraphAssigned and either TGraph2DAssigned or TGraph3DAssigned decorations. \
Generic tiling functions produce FoldedForm2D and/or FoldedForm3D tiles from \
the TGraph2DAssigned or TGraph3DAssigned decorations, though you can generate \
those directly if you wish.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.629974811897826*^9, 3.629974993414048*^9}, {
  3.6300103365891037`*^9, 3.6300103373772993`*^9}, {3.706911132307738*^9, 
  3.7069111338582683`*^9}, {3.706911179914609*^9, 3.706911209258811*^9}, {
  3.70775457482745*^9, 3.707754576218519*^9}, {3.707757235577754*^9, 
  3.7077572859543676`*^9}, {3.7077710972458286`*^9, 3.7077711071500187`*^9}, {
  3.7078377431289597`*^9, 
  3.707837765396718*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8a2156e0-a1cd-4d11-94b5-\
d1f22ea9c7d6"],

Cell["\<\
Note, though, that decorations FoldedForm2D and FoldedForm3D for tiles are \
only useful if the tile vertices of the folded form are geometrically similar \
to the vertices of the crease pattern because they will be placed on the same \
tiling. This is the case with the 2D twists in this and the next section.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707754578571031*^9, 3.707754595355048*^9}, {
  3.707771125742264*^9, 3.707771127358314*^9}, {3.707837790859641*^9, 
  3.707837807194673*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9b31d183-30d4-4cd9-b899-\
f1a0e0cfc7c6"],

Cell["\<\
If the tile vertices of the folded form are not geometrically similar to \
those of the crease pattern, then you should use the function \
MonolithicEmbedTiling (see below) to generate a monolithic version of the \
tiling and then fold it into the flat-folded or 3D shape.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707837822209751*^9, 
  3.707837903971694*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4181d86a-3002-4c85-b46e-\
d64bccb8f471"]
}, Closed]],

