Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Monolithic tilings", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707755087494379*^9, 
  3.707755090143073*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7e50489b-942e-4073-b424-\
471d80ab8375"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Monolithic graphs", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.630160673451483*^9, 3.630160692008222*^9}, 
   3.707761501343646*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d53739ca-1835-4931-b1c6-\
3ab468337261"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.630160694168374*^9, 
  3.630160694624448*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0ae2a8ea-1726-4b3d-9f3c-\
2315a880fe14"],

Cell["\<\
Normally when you create the CreasePattern or FoldedForm decorations, they \
are composed of many separate units that only look like \
they\[CloseCurlyQuote]re one big thing because both CP and FF extends \
precisely to the tile polygon boundaries and no further. This ends up looking \
fine in the interior of the pattern (usually), but that means that the edge \
of the paper may be incorrectly rendered in the folded form, since folded \
form tiles are usually not precisely the exact folded form of a crease \
pattern tile.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707761508687397*^9, 
  3.707761677937879*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f8a47519-1464-429f-a974-\
f8191f1541cf"],

Cell["\<\
If we want to render the folded form precisely so that it matches the crease \
pattern, then we should use one of the functions in this section, which merge \
individual tiles together into a single monolithic TGraphAssigned, \
TGraph2DAssigned, or TGraph3DAssigned, and then create the crease pattern or \
folded form from that.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7077616823295517`*^9, 3.707761733610486*^9}, {
  3.707836139164119*^9, 
  3.707836151091266*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7c7a60d6-4b88-4cfa-8aca-\
d9f4523a2e1c"],

Cell["\<\
This guarantees that the rendered folded form is correctly the folded form of \
the individual tiling. However, the merging process is costly (in terms of \
time).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707761742633636*^9, 
  3.707761790633879*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"58a2c86a-44e3-481b-b08a-\
ad5b13ecb014"],

Cell["\<\
Note that this process can be used to create folded form renderings of \
tilings where the individual tiles are not geometrically similar to their \
folded forms. It effectively simulates the manual process of creating a \
tiling-based tessellation; we create crease pattern tiles, glue them \
together, then fold up the result.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707762440647696*^9, 
  3.707762525577672*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"12ec9fb4-5db9-440e-ac4d-\
88ef47382d2d"],

Cell["\<\
You can accomplish the same thing without going through the Tiling \
infrastructure by using the functions MergeGraphs and JoinGraphs (and their \
descendants) directly if you are putting together small numbers of folded \
shapes.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707834041592412*^9, 
  3.7078341341212797`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3df1cd99-fe4c-4fd0-a277-\
5d5d61077a2c"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "MonolithicEmbedTiling[",
 StyleBox["tiling",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["decoration",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]\n\t(options) KillMergedEdges, SamePtTolerance, CollinearCleanup, \
CollinearTolerance"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707836457910186*^9, 3.707836486214754*^9}, 
   3.707836579658254*^9, 3.707864199882712*^9, {3.70786458374728*^9, 
   3.707864596183078*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"17c5bac3-77f1-4f8c-885a-\
31d58fda1823"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MonolithicEmbedTiling[",
 StyleBox["tiling",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["decoration",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] embeds a tiling as a single TGraph (or descendant) object by merging \
individual tiles."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707836500641687*^9, 3.707836546655613*^9}, {
  3.707836582304219*^9, 3.707836589239737*^9}, {3.707864436057443*^9, 
  3.707864451882566*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"959e06d2-152c-4f4b-bf68-\
a413686eea86"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Arguments:\n\t",
 StyleBox["tiling",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] a tiling\n\t",
 StyleBox["decoration",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] one of TGraphAssigned, TGraph2DAssigned, or TGraph3DAssigned."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7078365483022213`*^9, 3.7078366015280857`*^9}, 
   3.707837205659841*^9, {3.707839986416814*^9, 
   3.707839987229788*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"94ba086e-98ff-41ae-bdef-\
1d6da3f23bed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Options:\n\tKillMergedEdges \[Rule] True | False, specify whether to remove \
borders edges of tiles.\n\tSamePtTolerance \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["tol",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", tolerance on whether two vertices are distinct.\n\tCollinearCleanup \
\[Rule] True | False, specify whether to remove degree-2 vertices between \
collinear edges.\n\tCollinearTolerance \[Rule] tol, tolerance on whether two \
edges at degree-2 vertices are collinear."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707777850542234*^9, 3.707777853581541*^9}, {
   3.707778293920401*^9, 3.70777842795789*^9}, {3.707781820295705*^9, 
   3.707781862978016*^9}, 3.707823804527522*^9, 3.707824770447994*^9, 
   3.707824974120908*^9, {3.70782556161154*^9, 3.707825563363729*^9}, {
   3.707832655987712*^9, 3.707832669492002*^9}, {3.7078642049287176`*^9, 
   3.707864244948243*^9}, {3.707864602319542*^9, 
   3.707864652147869*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"22769f8d-f21c-4e3e-9906-\
6b86013c14eb"],

Cell["\<\
Returns a single TGraph+TAssigned descendant containing the merged graph.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707767605880972*^9, 3.707767608733931*^9}, {
  3.707836629321444*^9, 3.70783663542432*^9}, {3.7078400056288967`*^9, 
  3.707840019685636*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f611915b-2e8b-474a-808a-\
b70108d0cd50"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MonolithicEmbedTiling", "::", "baddec"}], 
   "=", "\"\<`1` is an invalid decoration for MonolithicEmbedTiling.\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707836972611849*^9, 3.707836987803102*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[2976]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e1847fb6-677c-4911-8eea-dcd63d08ab95"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CollinearCleanup", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<CollinearCleanup is an option to MonolithicEmbedTiling that \
specifies whether to remove degree-2 vertices between collinear edges.\>\""}],
   ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.707864289648345*^9, 3.707864314665286*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[2977]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ebac8c05-612f-4eb6-ad97-4e6dddc78f8b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Options", "[", "MonolithicEmbedTiling", "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"KillMergedEdges", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"CollinearCleanup", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]",
     "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.70786426106693*^9, 3.707864282607177*^9}, {
  3.707866252403682*^9, 3.707866260115268*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[2978]:=",ExpressionUUID->"32bdb7d2-b5c7-4487-910f-324e8da640f9"],

Cell["If we haven\[CloseCurlyQuote]t implemented a decoration, throw an \
error.", "Text",
