   3.627385976142639*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d54803a8-b7d6-46ff-9a89-\
44b4ce0d6232"],

Cell["\<\
There are regular polygons that make nice tilings if you combine them with \
triangles. Here we define a general unit triangle tile. Triangles in tilings \
are usually specified by their angles, rather than side length, so that\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s what we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll use here.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.627330288290827*^9, 3.627330351614819*^9}, {
   3.627331314977367*^9, 3.6273313466716013`*^9}, {3.6273317414780903`*^9, 
   3.6273317508378067`*^9}, 
   3.62738597614303*^9},ExpressionUUID->"06cb06cc-ddc5-4504-8692-\
cd963683f836"]
}, Closed]],

