Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Resch star tilings", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.64322534602533*^9, 
  3.643225351071033*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5a194ba1-95a8-47fe-86a4-\
f6f4e40fe560"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.643225352878798*^9, 
  3.643225353358815*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9b159a78-d0b1-4ad1-a2f5-\
20b66e15f788"],

Cell["\<\
In his patent 3,407,588, Ron Resch described a bunch of 3D structures that \
can be built upon certain classes of tilings of regular star polygons; they \
are those tilings in which every vertex contains exactly one star tip vertex \
and exactly one star reflex vertex for star polygons of order n=3 or higher. \
The possible tilings of that category are to be found in G&S, but not as a \
recognizable category, so I will call them \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Resch star \
tilings.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] They can be derived from k-uniform tilings, \
by recognizing that certain 2n-gons in the original tiling can be transformed \
into regular n-stars while preserving planarity of the tiling.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.643225357231024*^9, 3.643225363630438*^9}, {
  3.643225478450079*^9, 3.643225727584159*^9}, {3.643236040827822*^9, 
  3.6432360746717577`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"142dc84a-f162-4c28-ab6d-\
f7544e7208af"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "ReschStarName[",
 StyleBox["n",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]\nReschStarPatch[",
 StyleBox["n",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", \[Alpha]]\nReschStarPatchLatticeVectors[",
 StyleBox["n",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", \[Alpha]]"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.461389912865285*^9, 3.4613899140969276`*^9}, {
   3.617456136478376*^9, 3.617456139544603*^9}, 3.627385975537049*^9, {
   3.631294481966223*^9, 3.631294482981263*^9}, {3.643225988143108*^9, 
   3.64322598824434*^9}, 3.643226052501049*^9, {3.643226337619563*^9, 
