   3.701384796233676*^9},ExpressionUUID->"5e04b0b8-7c2f-44d0-953d-\
360f5370cf7f"],

Cell["\<\
This example shows how to build a woven tessellation from a graph of \
intersecting line segments.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6174775078537908`*^9, 3.617477517256857*^9}, {
  3.627769982923163*^9, 3.62777002113415*^9}, {3.627819221708824*^9, 
  3.627819288660655*^9}, {3.627825499643728*^9, 3.627825542401462*^9}, {
  3.627825600452413*^9, 3.62782560364353*^9}, {3.627825640553218*^9, 
  3.627825660856186*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f7bd9606-ba85-4803-a135-\
2459942ed02d"],

Cell["\<\
In this example, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll show the CP from the back side but \
the FF from the front. We make use of a trick to render the folded form: the \
last face built is one of the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]sliver\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] faces, so we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll use that index as \
the value of FaceupFace for a properly rendered flopped image.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.462809319434148*^9, 3.462809321873283*^9}, {
   3.462809427676667*^9, 3.462809476455744*^9}, {3.533605268078583*^9, 
