Cell["Alternating-wedge rotationally symmetric pots", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.651866656649942*^9, 3.651866664457019*^9}, {
  3.6518707939070673`*^9, 
  3.651870794390044*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fc286c9f-43eb-41aa-bcda-\
4fedd9b09e3a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Twisted radial rotationally symmetric pots", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.683801099067491*^9, 3.683801100165468*^9}, {
  3.686683348614529*^9, 3.686683384026902*^9}, {3.686951313350026*^9, 
  3.686951323431518*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"997a40da-0583-4400-9375-\
b5ec15a57dd9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.686767869386515*^9, 
  3.686767869912133*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"315f7c46-070f-4e92-9560-\
851f0b67715e"],

Cell["\<\
Here I design a modification of the thin-flange style of pot, in which we \
impart a helical twist to the body of the pot. Each successive horizontal \
cross section is somewhat rotated about the z axis relative to its \
predecessor. This has the byproduct effect of twisting the individual gores \
and flanges so that the gores wind helically around the pot. The exact amount \
of twist is not specified up front: rather, we specify a rotation angle \
\[Zeta] of the straight flange crease (relative to that of an untwisted pot), \
and that determines each of the successive cross sectional twists.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.683801102038966*^9, 3.683801134612908*^9}, {
  3.686683396442863*^9, 3.686683429216271*^9}, {3.686768202262047*^9, 
  3.686768211650908*^9}, {3.686771215594818*^9, 3.686771318193893*^9}, {
  3.686773776004197*^9, 3.686773792774362*^9}, {3.68695068818353*^9, 
  3.686950741269352*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0b6da7ce-c6f3-4a3c-bfd7-\
ffb9f7b8e32b"],

Cell["\<\
An effect of twisting the pot is that each of the gores also becomes somewhat \
twisted. In an untwisted pot, the gores are strips of quadrilaterals. that is \
also the case here, but now each quadrilateral is typically slightly bent \
along its diagonal (a la Thoki Yenn\[CloseCurlyQuote]s DNA molecule). Thus, \
this imparts an overall twist to each gore. The pot cross section should be \
coarsely polyhedral, not smoothly curved.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.686771329745953*^9, 3.68677145181727*^9}, {
  3.68695076661954*^9, 
  3.686950801464769*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2b8a7e96-aa26-4d11-a002-\
720d60d01603"],

Cell["\<\
Unlike the standard radial rotationally symmetric pot, it is not guaranteed \
that there is a faceted-flange solution for any cross section, and in \
general, the finer and smoother the polyhedral cross section, the smaller the \
range of possible body twist parameter. By setting PotFlatFlanges to \
PotFlatFlangesSmooth, you can often get a solution for the body but with \
smoothly curved flanges.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.686950806416874*^9, 3.686950904346553*^9}, {
  3.687016762387351*^9, 3.687016782273198*^9}, {3.6870168280463676`*^9, 
  3.687016855804284*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e161cdba-36c8-4b16-b617-\
b6fced4262f8"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "MakeTwistedPot[",
 StyleBox["pts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", \[Rho], \[Tau], \[Zeta]",
 StyleBox[", opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]\n\t(options) GoreTwist, TypeMinimumAngle, PotFlatFlanges, \
PotFlatFlangeInset, PotBorder, Options[PolygonalEllipse2D]\n\t\
PotFlatFlangesFaceted\n\t",
 "PotFlatFlangesSmooth"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5945835896833367`*^9, 3.594583608921858*^9}, {
   3.594584701789599*^9, 3.59458470205983*^9}, {3.594584772487775*^9, 
   3.594584773910712*^9}, {3.594664910992372*^9, 3.594664933686892*^9}, {
   3.594665079236754*^9, 3.594665082932379*^9}, 3.594678621668268*^9, {
   3.617903675942418*^9, 3.6179036982005877`*^9}, {3.650047579405183*^9, 
   3.65004758325141*^9}, 3.650047613280377*^9, {3.6500476627018557`*^9, 
   3.650047663125891*^9}, {3.650054143595581*^9, 3.650054165610414*^9}, {
   3.650064622973939*^9, 3.650064625685636*^9}, {3.650071736736527*^9, 
   3.65007173721875*^9}, {3.650110753646872*^9, 3.65011076338856*^9}, {
   3.650111560738832*^9, 3.650111562204171*^9}, 3.6502093570543756`*^9, {
   3.650288711294894*^9, 3.6502887430951357`*^9}, {3.650288785205056*^9, 
   3.650288785908465*^9}, {3.650288884022068*^9, 3.650288887277945*^9}, {
   3.65030302687268*^9, 3.6503030354027853`*^9}, {3.650303074348377*^9, 
   3.650303075151991*^9}, {3.683801622079706*^9, 3.683801627817796*^9}, {
   3.683819110409545*^9, 3.683819112274631*^9}, {3.686683445553219*^9, 
   3.686683449103022*^9}, {3.6867682800708733`*^9, 3.686768282134799*^9}, {
   3.686770391308689*^9, 3.686770393628659*^9}, 3.687013332136001*^9, {
   3.687013379114169*^9, 3.687013417890056*^9}, {3.687014359611395*^9, 
   3.687014372249291*^9}, {3.687016806100924*^9, 
   3.687016820351789*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9be32be3-3c4c-434f-a324-\
191c808d6b52"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MakeTwistedPot[",
 StyleBox["pts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", \[Rho], ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] takes a list of points ",
 StyleBox["pts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " defining a cross-section of a rotational pot with ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "-fold rotational symmetry and asymmetry factor \[Rho] and returns a \
TGraph3D+TAssigned describing a single wedge of the pot, both crease pattern \
and folded form. Arguments are:\n\t",
 StyleBox["pts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] a list of points in the x-z plane giving the exterior cross \
section. The first two points must have equal z-coordinate (flat bottom); the \
remainder should be strictly monotonic in z. The first point of ",
 StyleBox["pts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " should be {0,0}, but if it isn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll \
translate the cross section to the origin.\n\t",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the rotational symmetry.\n\t\[Rho] \[LongDash] an asymmetry \
factor, ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho] ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "=\[PlusMinus]1. It has this effect: for ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho] ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\[Rule] +1, the flanges point in the CCW direction (viewed from the top); \
for \[Dash]1, they point CW. Intermediate values are not supported. \n\t\
\[Tau], the gore twist factor, \[Tau] =\[PlusMinus]1, specifies the direction \
of folded diagonals on the gore quadrilaterals. For +1, the folded diagonals \
spiral outward CCW on the crease pattern; for \[Dash]1 they spiral outward \
CW. \n\t\[Zeta] \[LongDash] the rotation angle of the straight flange folds \
relative to those of an ordinary thin-flange pot. This value effectively \
specifies the degree of twisting of the pot.\nOptions are:\n\t\
TypeMinimumAngle \[Rule] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "min"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a962de86-a9df-4b51-93a8-a96ff245441d"],
 ", specifies the minimum fold angle that is assigned M or V. This is useful \
when we have very shallow angles going up the gores. This options is passed \
through to FoldAngleToType.\n\tPotFlatFlanges \[Rule] PotFlatFlangesFaceted | \
",
 "PotFlatFlangesSmooth",
 ", specifies whether to attempt to solve for facets on the flanges (which \
may or may not have a solution) or to not solve for any vertices along the \
flanges.\n\tPotFlatFlangeInset \[Rule] \[Epsilon], specifies a fractional \
inset toward the z-axis to be applied to the vertices on the inside of the \
flanges in 3D. This makes the renderer happy when rendering the 3D version, \
because it avoids coplanar facets.\n\tPotBorder \[Rule] PotPlanar | \
PotTrimmed. PotPlanar puts the boundary into a single plane. PotTrimmed trims \
the flange corners back to the last flange point, so that the final flange \
polygon is a triangle, not a square."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.594583620914513*^9, 3.594583712451603*^9}, {
   3.5945841191157427`*^9, 3.594584144471924*^9}, 3.594584713429246*^9, {
   3.594584779079007*^9, 3.594584810893369*^9}, {3.594585161806385*^9, 
   3.5945851903196163`*^9}, {3.594585321292512*^9, 3.5945853642580023`*^9}, {
   3.594585446884306*^9, 3.594585461394816*^9}, {3.594593332557025*^9, 
   3.594593343847333*^9}, 3.594598806391003*^9, {3.594652881856471*^9, 
   3.594652976312571*^9}, {3.594665041393795*^9, 3.5946650759317827`*^9}, {
   3.594678531075056*^9, 3.594678619564049*^9}, {3.615302088365167*^9, 
   3.615302091676679*^9}, {3.650034408267655*^9, 3.650034415496528*^9}, {
   3.650034506418766*^9, 3.650034541984724*^9}, {3.650034589197397*^9, 
   3.650034597589144*^9}, {3.650034644937892*^9, 3.650034648322154*^9}, {
   3.650035594335135*^9, 3.650035596613913*^9}, {3.650035676632546*^9, 
   3.650035684055887*^9}, {3.65003574449161*^9, 3.650035744915497*^9}, {
   3.6500476142283077`*^9, 3.650047673670881*^9}, {3.650052431521241*^9, 
   3.650052483598957*^9}, {3.650053858360255*^9, 3.650053889820717*^9}, {
   3.650053928267414*^9, 3.650053967479802*^9}, {3.6500646352691517`*^9, 
   3.65006470686545*^9}, {3.650110770988643*^9, 3.650110912125697*^9}, {
   3.650288751919765*^9, 3.650288951987486*^9}, {3.650303038347497*^9, 
   3.650303111807828*^9}, {3.651445152257967*^9, 3.651445156135133*^9}, {
   3.683801618584126*^9, 3.683801633371931*^9}, {3.683801675780724*^9, 
   3.683801765960191*^9}, {3.683807171070451*^9, 3.683807209479836*^9}, {
   3.683807298520892*^9, 3.683807320249282*^9}, {3.6838191200631638`*^9, 
   3.68381915762112*^9}, {3.683819189282358*^9, 3.683819192604112*^9}, {
   3.68668351173299*^9, 3.686683641551236*^9}, {3.686745403060246*^9, 
   3.686745412688728*^9}, 3.686765474223279*^9, 3.686767886296072*^9, {
   3.686767930031718*^9, 3.686767931805797*^9}, {3.6867682865993*^9, 
   3.686768366713996*^9}, {3.686768613322427*^9, 3.686768689559268*^9}, {
   3.686770399973341*^9, 3.686770450521154*^9}, {3.686772085099313*^9, 
   3.6867721553181343`*^9}, {3.687013424763472*^9, 3.687013461619852*^9}, {
   3.687013496481685*^9, 3.687013522191881*^9}, {3.687013560141246*^9, 
   3.687013578844479*^9}, {3.68701680614409*^9, 
   3.6870168203913393`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7cc919cd-dccd-47cf-9082-\
bfa593ea5487"],

Cell["\<\
Note that \[Rho], \[Tau], and \[Zeta] can be set independently. By giving \
\[Rho] and \[Zeta] the same sign, you can exaggerate the helicity of the \
flange edges; conversely, by giving them opposite sites, you can reduce the \
helicity to get the flange edges approximately vertical.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.686770930538666*^9, 
  3.686771030228057*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"12c735e3-8a1c-4581-87ab-\
b93d2fb9f11e"],

Cell["\<\
For option PotFlatFlanges \[Rule] PotFlatFlangesFaceted, we attempt to \
triangulate the facets to make flange folds coplanar with the body quad \
folds. If you make this choice, there is not a guaranteed solution for a \
given cross section (unlike the non-twisted radial algorithm). If an \
unsolvable situation arises, an error is thrown, indicating the index of the \
point at which the error occurred. The function may or may not return a TObj, \
but it will not have consistent vertex coordinates.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6869511304049873`*^9, 3.686951277762521*^9}, {
   3.6870135412403107`*^9, 3.687013678422529*^9}, {3.687013740465032*^9, 
   3.687013747448627*^9}, 
   3.687016806181694*^9},ExpressionUUID->"5887eff8-7c9c-4ebc-9de3-\
9bf3f6f6b9f4"],

Cell["\<\
On the other hand, if you choose PotFlatFlanges \[Rule] PotFlatFlangesSmooth, \
the flanges will have pro-forma unfolded creases across them and the 3D \
rendering won\[CloseCurlyQuote]t be isometrically correct. You can still \
probably fold the CP, but with smoothly curved facets.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.687013709750803*^9, 3.687013713426445*^9}, {
   3.687013745452804*^9, 3.687013794541687*^9}, {3.687013829779421*^9, 
   3.687013877800286*^9}, 
   3.687016820434554*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a9959769-2e79-477d-aad2-\
cf27b19fbc06"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"PotTrimmed", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<PotTrimmed is an option to MakeTwistedPot that specifies that \
the corners of the flanges should be trimmed off.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.686772166242936*^9, 3.686772213753969*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3504]:=",ExpressionUUID->"05629178-ebce-44fc-9bd9-1d656ed6e1c1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"PotFlatFlanges", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<PotFlatFlanges is an option to MakeTwistedPot that specifies \
whether the flanges should be faceted or smooth.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.687014376473392*^9, 3.687014402669154*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3505]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5d075594-6e11-4bf9-8908-95269ca1165a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"PotFlatFlangesFaceted", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<PotFlatFlangesFaceted is the value of option PotFlatFlanges that \
specifies to try to solve for vertices on the facets that make them folded.\>\
\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.687014306778342*^9, 3.687014346312016*^9}, {
  3.687016806204534*^9, 3.687016806224407*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3506]:=",ExpressionUUID->"102db940-98e7-49e8-b930-0157fd876563"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"PotFlatFlangesSmooth", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<PotFlatFlangesSmooth is the value of option PotFlatFlanges that \
specifies to let the flanges be smooth.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.687014410792584*^9, 3.687014433827577*^9}, {
  3.687016820457501*^9, 3.687016820473611*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3507]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3edaca97-c161-494d-8d58-db7808fd8e6c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MakeTwistedPot", "::", "badrho"}], 
   "=", "\"\<`1` should be \[PlusMinus]1.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.686703567886604*^9, 3.686703583899192*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3508]:=",ExpressionUUID->"785c3bf6-376d-407a-ac8c-4823ceb60643"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MakeTwistedPot", "::", "badtau"}], 
   "=", "\"\<`1` should be \[PlusMinus]1.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.686703567886604*^9, 3.686703583899192*^9}, {
  3.686770523188477*^9, 3.686770525132696*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3509]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7336286f-512b-4c8b-b0bf-830124dc860e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MakeTwistedPot", "::", "badbord"}], 
   "=", "\"\<Option PotBorder\[Rule]`1` should be either PotPlanar or \
PotTrimmed.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.686703567886604*^9, 3.686703583899192*^9}, {
  3.686770523188477*^9, 3.686770525132696*^9}, {3.68677281843884*^9, 
  3.686772867697258*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3510]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f1924b18-c911-49ba-8815-03553e363d34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MakeTwistedPot", "::", "notflat"}], 
   "=", "\"\<Cross section `1` does not have equal z-coordinates for the \
first two points.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.683825704227743*^9, 3.683825742432519*^9}, 
   3.6866836439958353`*^9, 3.686683697787023*^9, {3.68668396354504*^9, 
   3.686684013095241*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3511]:=",ExpressionUUID->"34b4e72c-cac9-4e8b-bfa0-d35208023866"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MakeTwistedPot", "::", "badpts"}], 
   "=", "\"\<Cross section `1` is not strictly monotonic in z.\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.683825704227743*^9, 3.683825742432519*^9}, {
   3.683827769144491*^9, 3.683827795832732*^9}, 3.686683645583271*^9, 
