Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Twist-joined and offset tubes", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671178633802772*^9, 3.671178647495239*^9}, {
   3.671290900373554*^9, 3.671290904283613*^9}, {3.673097032845635*^9, 
   3.673097034835564*^9}, 
   3.6731039251728487`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"9da1d063-8cdb-4d29-aac3-\
6852bb4e60c9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671178664673807*^9, 
  3.671178665076703*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3b8d84eb-bd72-45b1-994b-\
d9e706255e8a"],

Cell["\<\
Rebecca Gieseking developed a bunch of amazing designs that have the \
appearance of a cylinder, sliced diagonally, and then the two halves offset \
from one another\[LongDash]all folded from a single sheet of paper. This \
section computes the joint structure for such offsets, which are realized by \
a type of 3D twist that is a generalization of the bistable Yoshimura twist \
tube.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671178666764154*^9, 3.671178753735621*^9}, {
  3.6711788081999826`*^9, 3.671178871702298*^9}, {3.671290924824925*^9, 
  3.671290933044715*^9}, {3.6713632911007633`*^9, 
  3.6713633041717157`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ecf187d3-e3b4-4a79-ab19-\
ccdb60665f7e"],

Cell["\<\
Remarkably, with cylindrical tubes, the twist surfaces are planar, and an \
offset translates into a tilt in the twist surface, giving rise to the \
appearance of a diagonal slice. In fact, the diagonal slice arises as a \
natural byproduct of creating the offset. For non-cylindrical tube shapes, \
the twist interfaces are non-planar.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671363310396206*^9, 3.67136338777358*^9}, {
  3.675089591624178*^9, 
  3.6750895920877247`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4ef34533-5538-40f6-ab2c-\
5796302f6b33"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Twist-topped tubes", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671362168888173*^9, 
  3.6713621721430187`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"990483ab-57e6-4068-ad99-\
9e5f4f5d19d9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671362175175549*^9, 
  3.671362175598803*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"22871dfd-fa56-4cf2-b0c3-\
c1e3e13d7dbb"],

Cell["\<\
If we make a tube with a polygonal cross section, we can close its top with a \
twist and can arbitrarily choose the points of pleat convergence and the \
angle of the top of the twist relative to the axis of the tube.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671362180742323*^9, 3.671362241594655*^9}, {
  3.6713623284322853`*^9, 3.6713623305829577`*^9}, {3.67310303490016*^9, 
  3.673103036075601*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3a1d4b51-4f9f-4474-86ff-\
f99004eb09cd"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "ClosedTwistToppedTube[",
 StyleBox["pts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["ctr",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["dir",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]\n\t(options) TwistDirection, TubeHeight, PanelOverlap, PleatExtension, \
TypeMinimumAngle, TypeMaximumAngle"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671362336662366*^9, 3.671362416353313*^9}, {
   3.671362467558424*^9, 3.671362475109674*^9}, {3.671362627093939*^9, 
   3.671362629012062*^9}, {3.671371003836982*^9, 3.67137100473036*^9}, {
   3.671458439560089*^9, 3.6714584432711163`*^9}, {3.671530386347212*^9, 
   3.671530393616667*^9}, 3.673100525059291*^9, {3.6754416404105473`*^9, 
   3.675441643930232*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"832f6eaa-97f4-45bb-85cb-\
a8114daee877"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "ClosedTwistToppedTube[",
 StyleBox["pts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["ctr",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["dir",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["opts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] constructs a tube topped with a conical closed twist. Arguments are:\n\t\
",
 StyleBox["pts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] a list of 2D points defining the cross section of the twist.\n\
\t",
 StyleBox["ctr",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the point of convergence of the pleats, as a 3D point.\n\t",
 StyleBox["dir",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the normal vector of the planar surface of the twist.\nOptions \
are:\n\tTwistDirection \[Rule] CCW | CW, specifies the direction of the \
pleats of the twist.\n\tTubeHeight \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", specifies the height of the tube\n\tPanelOverlap \[Rule] True | False, \
specifiles whether to add an extra panel to the right\n\tTwistExtension \
\[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["d",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", an amount to extend/reduce the q- and r-lines beyond the point of \
convergence.\n\tTypeMinimumAngle, TypeMaximumAngle are passed through to \
ReassignGraph3D.\nIt returns a TGraph3D+TAssigned that describes the crease \
pattern and folded form."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6713623706036*^9, 3.671362374963769*^9}, {
   3.671362432223959*^9, 3.671362559456608*^9}, {3.6713626337326307`*^9, 
   3.671362777443411*^9}, {3.671363119958619*^9, 3.671363130302281*^9}, {
   3.671363965292608*^9, 3.671364105977175*^9}, {3.671371010674608*^9, 
   3.671371016017742*^9}, {3.671458446855494*^9, 3.6714585122681823`*^9}, {
   3.671530401898724*^9, 3.671530411055305*^9}, {3.671530483342757*^9, 
   3.6715304859305553`*^9}, {3.6715319480056076`*^9, 3.671531950773385*^9}, 
   3.673100525121285*^9, {3.67310065465338*^9, 3.6731006553329287`*^9}, {
   3.673102947123313*^9, 3.67310296928825*^9}, {3.6731030039501967`*^9, 
   3.673103022013321*^9}, {3.675441653797927*^9, 
   3.675441662641305*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"333d1c3f-2e30-4181-afc0-\
1354a71551f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The plane of the twist is the plane perpendicular to vector ",
 StyleBox["dir",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that passes through {0,0,0}. Thus, if you give a ",
 StyleBox["z",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "-coordinate of ",
 StyleBox["ctr",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that is 0, the twist will be planar; if it is greater than 0, the twist \
will be pyramidal with a planar base."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671364095499913*^9, 3.671364097091387*^9}, {
  3.6731007064573526`*^9, 
  3.673100727735352*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c9eff5ed-c667-42ca-a0c4-\
11cfbe4dbf19"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TubeHeight", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<TubeHeight is an option to TwistJoinedTubes that specifies the \
heights of the top and bottom cylinders.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6711792830786333`*^9, 3.671179302527566*^9}, 
   3.671290969828333*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3558]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f76d346b-e9f2-4a5f-a9f0-4ff85e86979f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"PanelOverlap", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<PanelOverlap is an option to TwistJoinedTubes that specifies \
whether to add an extra panel that overlaps the first.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6713329064203453`*^9, 3.671332966297659*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3559]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a0e0d956-52a8-4c9a-928f-0b96f3ec3c3b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TwistExtension", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<TwistExtension is an option to ClosedTwistToppedTube that \
specifies a distance to extend the twist folds beyond the point of \
convergence.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671458499770525*^9, 3.671458545371141*^9}, 
   3.673100525140369*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3560]:=",ExpressionUUID->"959ad561-177e-4b4d-9525-569e992ee74b"],

Cell["\<\
Note that we change the default value of TypeMaximumAngle to something less \
than 180\[Degree], because know we will definitely have flat-folded creases.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671531993755661*^9, 
  3.671532022448866*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"176b815a-c274-4d2f-8514-\
e32f727c0b0e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Options", "[", "ClosedTwistToppedTube", "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"TwistDirection", "\[Rule]", "CCW"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"TubeHeight", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"PanelOverlap", "\[Rule]", "False"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"TwistExtension", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"TypeMinimumAngle", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"TypeMaximumAngle", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"89", "\[Degree]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.671363013536831*^9, 3.671363039987505*^9}, 
   3.671371024520961*^9, {3.671458490975281*^9, 3.671458519023294*^9}, {
   3.671531909106469*^9, 3.671531941950986*^9}, 3.6731005251642017`*^9, {
   3.675441668808995*^9, 3.675441670070459*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3561]:=",ExpressionUUID->"dce05661-bee9-4c5c-83da-50d128ac2de0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClosedTwistToppedTube", "[", 
   RowBox[{"pts_List", ",", 
    RowBox[{"ctr_List", ":", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
