Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Curved folding", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.668362598229488*^9, 3.668362608932678*^9}, 
   3.6924566882904997`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"53013e41-7b99-4582-87a1-\
a71ec90b65d9"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["0. SETUP",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799974616738443*^9, 
  3.799974635500642*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1ce5ee96-77cd-43bc-96e0-\
22aeb92e1380"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Background", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.668955957130957*^9, 3.668955957617339*^9}, {
  3.799532795619906*^9, 
  3.799532798748595*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b369488f-1e17-4a81-a1a0-\
1926331df83b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799532785332891*^9, 
  3.799532785766333*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7a1eb67a-7476-43b4-8bef-\
64fad7d8caf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This section addresses folds that are continuously varying smooth (at least \
piecewise) curves. We use a different representation than \
we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve used for discrete (polyhedral) structures. Rather than \
2D and 3D vectors to represent the CP and FF, we use scalar- and \
vector-valued functions (pure functions, in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ") to describe the curves."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6689559595768023`*^9, 3.668956047884961*^9}, {
  3.687477464290483*^9, 3.6874774797575502`*^9}, {3.797442953471663*^9, 
  3.797442955589755*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bca94307-2d39-4d7b-a69e-\
75ffa5197b24"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Analytic and numerical functions", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799532754632588*^9, 
  3.799532760938422*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fae9ca84-5d0c-412d-a7ae-\
6b0b849faefd"],

Cell["\<\
Most functions come in two versions: an analytic version, which attempts to \
evaluate symbolic expressions, and a numerical version, which uses \
InterpolatingFunctions over a specified domain.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799511616482426*^9, 
  3.799511657715371*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cbdb1f6a-f054-4a61-962e-\
526cca111978"],

Cell["\<\
As in Mathematica, the numeric version will be prefixed with N (e.g., DSolve \
vs NDSolve). And in general, the numeric version will take the same arguments \
as the analytic version, but with an additional domain specification and \
different options.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799511661450943*^9, 3.7995117301559076`*^9}, {
  3.799532931422419*^9, 
  3.799532940153483*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7d6101e0-8a2b-4af6-afb9-\
7fbbeba61db4"],

Cell["\<\
Analytic functions typically accept the options Simplification and \
Assumptions, which lets you specify simplification that happens in \
sequentially constructed functions. Since DSolve is used internally to find \
solutions to the differential equations, some also accept Options[DSolve] as \
options.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799399565904958*^9, 3.799399610882998*^9}, {
  3.799399645972166*^9, 
  3.799399685000971*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"35e99f93-9b7a-49c7-85b1-\
3d784dfdab38"],

Cell["\<\
Because Mathematica is pretty darned good at solving differential equations, \
I\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll use DSolve and NDSolve even if there is a solution \
possible with sequential integration (for example, the fold angle integral, \
or differential equations solvable via turning angle substitution).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799532625466894*^9, 
  3.799532729589309*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3915db63-c9fb-4545-bacb-\
52b86ebccea3"],

Cell["\<\
Numerically defined continuous functions are represented by \
InterpolatingFunction objects for scalar functions and by vector-valued pure \
functions whose components are InterpolatingFunction objects.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.691505042033193*^9, 3.69150508329802*^9}, {
  3.6920604769164343`*^9, 
  3.692060476952055*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dce5b194-32bc-4a8d-97e5-\
79f2dedd259e"],

Cell["\<\
Numeric function typically accept Options[NDSolve] and \
Options[FunctionInterpolation] as options.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799399629681512*^9, 3.7993996381781263`*^9}, {
  3.799399688698414*^9, 
  3.799399725424288*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cbbd81b3-c5b2-4133-bde6-\
d942c3f4b00a"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Functions, lists of functions, and lists of rules", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799532825988337*^9, 
  3.799532831968266*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3918c216-b054-43a4-bc96-\
33bb7854bda3"],

Cell["\<\
Some functions in this section return other functions or lists of other \
functions: for example, CurveSpeed.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.79939975186571*^9, 
  3.799399798072893*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d56e2310-5feb-4ab3-9852-\
a4542ab2ff73"],

Cell["\<\
Other functions in this section construct long lists of functions: these have \
names of the form *System, and return a list of rules that contain a family \
of associated functions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.691505089921455*^9, 3.691505131371585*^9}, {
  3.6915051639552183`*^9, 3.6915051803316708`*^9}, {3.7993997416361647`*^9, 
  3.7993997421291323`*^9}, {3.799399803413465*^9, 3.799399819098314*^9}, {
  3.799532853640574*^9, 
  3.799532855344176*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c49a064-c222-4b66-8ebc-\
e56aa246a122"],

Cell["\<\
This \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]list of rules\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] idiom is \
halfway to the concept of a Tessellatica object (which is implemented \
internally as such a list of rules). At some point we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll \
probably convert these to full-fledged Tessellatica objects.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.691505182669763*^9, 
  3.691505229926913*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6b0cf403-4a39-4b01-9cf6-\
baa36d574204"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Simplification in analytic functions", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799510044487734*^9, 
  3.799510048191587*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a12ed1d4-729e-4747-a65d-\
3b591013c7d7"],

Cell["\<\
For analytic functions, even though we\[CloseCurlyQuote]re working with pure \
functions, we can perform algebraic simplifications by applying a \
simplification function at successive stages of the evaluation. So we will \
see things like:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503321432422*^9, 
  3.799503399801322*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e14514b1-a420-4bae-913a-\
d636fafee11f"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["f = Functionize[s, expr // sfn]", "Input"]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503402770591*^9, 3.79950341696949*^9}, {
  3.799503459248877*^9, 3.799503459689392*^9}, {3.7995036827874327`*^9, 
  3.799503683109127*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"aaca709f-40f2-443e-bc23-\
00adf7b4e784"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 StyleBox["sfn",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a simplification function, ",
 StyleBox["s",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a parameter, and ",
 StyleBox["expr",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is some function of ",
 StyleBox["s",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or combination of functions applied to ",
 StyleBox["s",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503418961563*^9, 3.7995034767533917`*^9}, {
  3.799503680833911*^9, 3.799503686851063*^9}, {3.7995330250276*^9, 
  3.799533026188801*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f56c013f-438f-4977-be7a-\
934eb7cceb90"],

Cell["\<\
For numerical functions, no simplification is needed, so the corresponding \
entry will be\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.79950348008075*^9, 
  3.799503494370061*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a053e010-fd03-46c7-83db-\
d5b9034d0efa"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["f = Functionize[s, expr]", "Input"]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7995034963935347`*^9, 3.7995035043775887`*^9}, {
  3.79950369493034*^9, 
  3.799503695299937*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c1ee11ef-03ec-4939-bfae-\
3edd6493bda6"],

Cell["\<\
Observe that the syntax  Functionize[s, expr] is the same as that of \
Function[s, expr], and they both produce a pure function as a result. \
However, while Function holds all its arguments unevaluated, Functionize will \
attempt to evaluate its arguments to the extent possible, and will apply the \
simplification function and any algebraic operations applied inside of it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.79950351156111*^9, 
  3.79950359825849*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c48f7007-7109-4c3f-b2a8-\
a174d5c74976"],

Cell["\<\
For numerical functions, the building blocks are InterpolatingFunction \
objects, which can be algebraically manipulated like ordinary functions. It \
is possible to wrap Function around InterpolatingFunction objects; we do this \
to implement vector-valued functions that are constructed from \
interpolations. See the documentation of function FunctionInterpolationAlt \
for more details of that.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503602539769*^9, 3.799503665835457*^9}, {
   3.799533061784403*^9, 3.7995331208834147`*^9}, 
   3.801733049987854*^9},ExpressionUUID->"33278b7b-9d17-4595-b722-\
b62789c0a070"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["InterpolatingFunctionCount growth in numerical functions", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7995056876566257`*^9, 3.799505710193748*^9}, 
   3.799532770820815*^9, {3.801733098857228*^9, 
   3.801733102462919*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"019d4a02-1fea-4a68-adc6-\
af7bff887e25"],

Cell["\<\
One of the things to watch out for in numerical functions is the exponential \
growth in the number of leaves in subexpressions when sequential \
subexpressions are built from InterpolatingFunction objects. See this example.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799505696765717*^9, 3.79950577633079*^9}, {
  3.799505806650442*^9, 3.799505841306964*^9}, {3.799506197412465*^9, 
  3.7995061992934713`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9a00a312-803f-4fe8-9315-\
4d599acdc10e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"s", ",", "f", ",", "g", ",", "h", ",", "k"}], "}"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FunctionInterpolationAlt", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", 
          SuperscriptBox["s", "2"]}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"s", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"PrintThis", "[", 
      RowBox[{"InterpolatingFunctionCount", "[", "f", "]"}], "]"}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"g", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Functionize", "[", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"f", "[", "s", "]"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"Mag", "[", 
          RowBox[{"f", "[", "s", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"PrintThis", "[", 
      RowBox[{"InterpolatingFunctionCount", "[", "g", "]"}], "]"}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"h", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Functionize", "[", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"g", "[", "s", "]"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"Mag", "[", 
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "s", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"PrintThis", "[", 
      RowBox[{"InterpolatingFunctionCount", "[", "h", "]"}], "]"}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"k", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FunctionInterpolationAlt", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"h", "[", "s", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"s", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"PrintThis", "[", 
      RowBox[{"InterpolatingFunctionCount", "[", "k", "]"}], "]"}], ";"}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "//", "ShowExample"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799505846022076*^9, 3.799505984244322*^9}, {
  3.799506146248679*^9, 3.799506171110657*^9}, {3.799524036228301*^9, 
  3.799524040209157*^9}, {3.801732410745407*^9, 3.801732508286521*^9}, {
  3.801732571852872*^9, 3.801732608507608*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3598]:=",ExpressionUUID->"65df3ecf-e515-40f9-b448-39c5b3b8b7ab"],

Cell["\<\
Although f contains just two InterpolatingFunction objects, g contains six (3 \
copies each of the two components of f). Further sequential products \
involving g can lead to rapid expansion in the number of \
InterpolatingFunction objects distributed within subexpressions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799506008831643*^9, 3.799506133684854*^9}, {
  3.799506193261438*^9, 3.7995061947328043`*^9}, {3.8017325453301086`*^9, 
  3.8017325588813963`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8b52bb80-ac32-4ed4-9e12-\
077acbaa7dee"],

Cell["\<\
So, one can periodically reinterpolate (as in k), which will evaluate all the \
copies scattered through g and collapse back down to a simpler expression \
containing fewer InterpolatingFunction subexpressions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799506211876878*^9, 3.799506271614219*^9}, {
   3.799506324749414*^9, 3.7995063410138397`*^9}, 
   3.8017326232017527`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a1cfa7e2-fabe-47d5-830e-\
52d6a3e4ef23"],

Cell["\<\
In general, most functions that return InterpolatingFunction objects will \
perform a reinterpolation so that the returned functions are as small as \
possible.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799507559334337*^9, 3.799507594598207*^9}, {
  3.799533174125452*^9, 
  3.7995331942361097`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f4a0e6c1-4fe3-49a7-815b-\
3f582ea3e868"],

Cell["\<\
There is a bit of an art to reinterpolation of intermediate results, because \
there is a loss of accuracy with each reinterpolation. One should \
reinterpolate just often enough to keep the expressions tractable. Judicious \
use of LeafCount and/or InterpolatingFunctionCount during development can \
identify when cascaded objects are getting too large.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7995063427257986`*^9, 3.799506442103965*^9}, {
  3.799508300383009*^9, 3.799508312923299*^9}, {3.79950876329596*^9, 
  3.799508778069767*^9}, {3.799533206719564*^9, 
  3.799533249433133*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"48960571-7b99-4ea5-8b9c-\
d4fffa5a2103"],

Cell["\<\
A good strategy for creating the numerical function is to first set up the \
function entirely with Functionize (as above), and then after each \
subexpression of the form\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799509549110214*^9, 3.799509825318594*^9}, {
  3.799509860086652*^9, 3.7995100127832627`*^9}, {3.7995119269655747`*^9, 
  3.799511994188959*^9}, {3.799524047056734*^9, 3.799524053680422*^9}, {
  3.799533257636963*^9, 
  3.79953326882045*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b013bfe9-66c2-40f8-bab3-\
1904a0a1f252"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["f = Functionize[s, expr]", "Input"]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799533271522126*^9, 
  3.799533277305379*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"17364a17-62cf-4b31-97d1-\
27fc414a1828"],

Cell["insert the call ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7995332800094852`*^9, 
  3.799533285394329*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5a84281b-8cca-4369-a48f-\
9413200a0437"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["PrintThis[InterpolatingFunctionCount[f]]", "Input"]], \
"Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799533287351571*^9, 
  3.7995332925634212`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"232f6c95-2ac7-46b1-8961-\
249c2ae41555"],

Cell["\<\
which will echo the number of InterpolatingFunction objects currently in the \
expression. If it looks too large, then replace the Functionize call with\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799533294536096*^9, 3.799533300881453*^9}, {
  3.801732344858411*^9, 
  3.801732345391465*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ba0cb26d-7eec-4366-b8de-\
ea6cf0a14978"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["FunctionInterpolationAlt[expr, {x, u0, u1}, opts]", \
"Input"]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7995333062882*^9, 3.7995333112827806`*^9}, 
   3.8017323541450453`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"6ff2026d-d50b-400a-9889-\
44751bc8ae95"],

Cell["\<\
Note that options for FunctionInterpolationAlt can be passed through \
unfiltered, because both ignore any options that don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
pertain to it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799533328037819*^9, 3.7995333503004713`*^9}, {
  3.8017323671842403`*^9, 
  3.80173237139225*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a8b69d73-3508-4902-a8e2-\
79403e3b59f5"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Derivatives and interpolating functions", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7995039338935*^9, 3.799503936460636*^9}, {
  3.7995058137464437`*^9, 3.799505817226965*^9}, {3.799507614343155*^9, 
  3.799507614542427*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6f40926c-bb29-49f4-b663-\
68bd041e9dba"],

Cell["\<\
We can take derivatives of pure functions, and the derivatives get applied to \
the contents of the function.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503939636026*^9, 3.799503974669096*^9}, {
  3.7995333687817173`*^9, 
  3.799533369038838*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cf243154-2bc4-4e1d-a769-\
0d37c2bdd84e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "f", "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "=", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "#", "]"}], "&"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"f", "'"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "//", 
  "ShowExample"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503800605873*^9, 3.799503830916547*^9}, {
  3.799503988127474*^9, 3.799503989821045*^9}, {3.799524064330811*^9, 
  3.799524066353234*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3599]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8bcefe82-46ae-4059-9de9-ea270ceb599b"],

Cell["\<\
Same thing for InterpolatingFunctions. Derivatives applied to \
InterpolatingFunctions are reinterpolated to create a new \
InterpolatingFunction.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799504005317887*^9, 3.79950402741414*^9}, {
  3.7995050052283382`*^9, 3.799505009428553*^9}, {3.799533379730139*^9, 
  3.799533392171453*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"31ef2972-0804-4e45-81c6-\
1bd4a04fccde"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"s", ",", "f"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FunctionInterpolation", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "s", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"s", ",", "0", ",", "\[Pi]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"f", "'"}], "]"}], ";"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "//", 
  "ShowExample"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503800605873*^9, 3.799503858613059*^9}, {
  3.799524069379912*^9, 3.799524071257024*^9}, {3.799524172308874*^9, 
  3.799524172450861*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3600]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b69170ae-f30f-4d68-907a-33ae7a8b281e"],

Cell["\<\
But if we wrap an InterpolatingFunction inside of another Function and then \
differentiate, the derivative is not taken inside.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799505099742106*^9, 3.799505120869564*^9}, {
  3.799533405364423*^9, 
  3.799533416826156*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"57c96b6b-a322-47fd-a69a-\
d590f9b1aec3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"s", ",", "f", ",", "g", ",", "h"}], "}"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FunctionInterpolation", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "s", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"s", ",", "0", ",", "\[Pi]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<f = \>\"", ",", "f"}], "]"}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "Derivatives", " ", "are", " ", "taken", " ", "inside", " ", "of", " ", 
       "an", " ", "InterpolatingFunction"}], " ", "*)"}], 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<f' = \>\"", ",", 
       RowBox[{"f", "'"}]}], "]"}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"g", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Functionize", "[", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", 
        RowBox[{"f", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
       "But", " ", "if", " ", "we", " ", "apply", " ", "the", " ", 
        "derivative", " ", "to", " ", "a", " ", "function", " ", "containing",
         " ", "an", " ", "InterpolatingFunction"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"it", "'"}], "s", " ", "not", " ", "taken", " ", "inside"}]}],
       " ", "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<g' = \>\"", ",", 
       RowBox[{"g", "'"}]}], "]"}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"If", " ", "we", " ", "re"}], "-", 
        RowBox[{
        "functionize", " ", "to", " ", "apply", " ", "the", " ", 
         "function"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "then", " ", "the", " ", "derivative", " ", "can", " ", "come", " ", 
        "inside"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"h", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Functionize", "[", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"g", "'"}], "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<h = \>\"", ",", "h"}], "]"}], ";"}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "//", "ShowExample"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503800605873*^9, 3.799503858613059*^9}, {
  3.799505081879447*^9, 3.799505091686173*^9}, {3.7995051707690067`*^9, 
  3.799505176335945*^9}, {3.799505214792713*^9, 3.799505416928709*^9}, {
  3.799505458752367*^9, 3.799505501900203*^9}, {3.799524076548276*^9, 
  3.799524078609465*^9}, {3.799524147653417*^9, 3.79952414783534*^9}, {
  3.8017326956049347`*^9, 3.80173269844331*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3601]:=",ExpressionUUID->"df52843b-f733-43a4-b710-997d5fd57c8b"],

Cell["\<\
So, if we create a FunctionInterpolationAlt and then differentiate, the \
derivatives are not applied to the contents.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799505521472241*^9, 3.799505545056855*^9}, 
   3.801732711571417*^9},ExpressionUUID->"26fcd718-da43-494c-a003-\
99abc28f7ff8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"s", ",", "f", ",", "g"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FunctionInterpolationAlt", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "s", "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"s", ",", "0", ",", "\[Pi]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<f' = \>\"", ",", 
       RowBox[{"f", "'"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "//",
   "ShowExample"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503800605873*^9, 3.799503858613059*^9}, {
   3.79950405941572*^9, 3.799504059766835*^9}, {3.799504927859626*^9, 
   3.7995049364211693`*^9}, {3.7995055894046097`*^9, 3.799505591656991*^9}, {
   3.799524082716748*^9, 3.799524084609069*^9}, {3.799524150836919*^9, 
   3.799524151002183*^9}, 3.801732714302857*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3602]:=",ExpressionUUID->"92f1dbb8-d390-4412-9c3b-24cdfa0b48f6"],

Cell["\<\
But if we re-Functionize as in this example, then the derivative will be \
applied.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799524128345399*^9, 
  3.7995241658576*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2cefc31f-dcda-4a56-8ec0-a588141b3e2d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"s", ",", "f", ",", "g"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FunctionInterpolationAlt", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "s", "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"s", ",", "0", ",", "\[Pi]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<f' = \>\"", ",", 
       RowBox[{"f", "'"}]}], "]"}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"g", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Functionize", "[", 
       RowBox[{"s", ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"f", "'"}], "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<g = \>\"", ",", "g"}], "]"}], ";"}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "//", "ShowExample"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.799503800605873*^9, 3.799503858613059*^9}, {
   3.79950405941572*^9, 3.799504059766835*^9}, {3.799504927859626*^9, 
   3.7995049364211693`*^9}, {3.799504968062974*^9, 3.799504977132937*^9}, {
   3.799505570646652*^9, 3.799505623865404*^9}, {3.799524087460794*^9, 
   3.799524089289363*^9}, {3.799524156179751*^9, 3.799524156338627*^9}, 
   3.801732717095717*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3603]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e83fa8b7-9e11-4df9-ac1d-dba4d93d322d"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Vector colors", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672099588909713*^9, 
  3.672099611463624*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"44ee08ad-27f5-40b5-aa77-\
f2ac17c61fe3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672099613871349*^9, 
  3.672099614279238*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ca32a1c6-ff7f-4148-b25a-\
17bda30523f3"],

Cell["Adopt some standard colors for common vectors.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6720996157434587`*^9, 3.672099623198917*^9}, {
  3.672101094732152*^9, 3.672101142775941*^9}, {3.672101201180155*^9, 
  3.67210131434899*^9}, {3.69150587758416*^9, 3.6915058810194607`*^9}, {
  3.691506431422496*^9, 
  3.691506446062021*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9bfa1baf-c729-442e-844e-\
b806d994bfa4"],

Cell["\<\
For the Frenet frame, we choose primary colors (tangent=Red, normal=Green, \
binormal=Blue). For the left normal, we just choose a darker shade of green. \
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.69150643962094*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ec8acdab-1bdd-42a4-a492-a126be430e9d"],

Cell["\<\
For the Darboux frame, we choose colors rotated slightly in the hue palette, \
but matched as follows: 
\tnormal\[LeftRightArrow]tangent normal, 
\tbinormal\[LeftRightArrow]surface normal, 
so that for a curved line on a curved surface, the Darboux frame converges to \
the Frenet frame as the surface flattens out.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.691506433503524*^9, 
  3.691506468249317*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6150e5b0-a3be-4d23-aed5-\
4f80e510d4e2"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
CurveVectorStyle
TangentVectorColor
NormalVectorColor
LeftNormalVectorColor
BinormalVectorColor
SurfaceNormalVectorColor
TangentNormalVectorColor
DirectorVectorColor\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100355483317*^9, 3.672100388167187*^9}, 
   3.691505933822547*^9, 3.6915068323038063`*^9, {3.80053408378878*^9, 
   3.8005340845498953`*^9}, {3.800534660448295*^9, 
   3.800534674912022*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"293cab9e-9c0b-4ecc-8f69-\
5aa157274e38"],

Cell["\<\
CurveVectorStyle is a list of rules that defines vector colors as CMYK colors \
(suitable for print).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100402288322*^9, 3.672100438572094*^9}, 
   3.691505933851894*^9, 
   3.691506832337688*^9},ExpressionUUID->"56108a38-2c58-4b2d-94b2-\
f4a0bc347790"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TangentVectorColor", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<TangentVectorColor is a color directive that defines the color \
for a tangent vector of a parameterized curve in 2D or 3D.\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100451587705*^9, 3.672100478877387*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3604]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4ece7ad7-d88e-4b21-bf66-74cb0ac0b657"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"NormalVectorColor", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<NormalVectorColor is a color directive that defines the color \
for a normal vector of a parameterized curve in 2D or 3D.\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100451587705*^9, 3.672100493874409*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3605]:=",ExpressionUUID->"06561272-0c18-4adf-905f-baf8d5cf46a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"LeftNormalVectorColor", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<LeftNormalVectorColor is a color directive that defines the \
color for theleft normal vector of a parameterized curve in 2D.\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100451587705*^9, 3.67210051572836*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3606]:=",ExpressionUUID->"33fc457b-9291-4265-8fe8-e888492fec5e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"BinormalVectorColor", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<BinormalVectorColor is a color directive that defines the color \
for the binormal vector of a parameterized curve in 3D.\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100451587705*^9, 3.672100493874409*^9}, {
  3.672100524516594*^9, 3.672100534583245*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3607]:=",ExpressionUUID->"241889e9-64b1-447d-8c04-0a71fb8ea5ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SurfaceNormalVectorColor", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<SurfaceNormalVectorColor is a color directive that defines the \
color for the surface normal vector of a parameterized surface or curve on a \
surface in 3D.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100451587705*^9, 3.672100493874409*^9}, {
  3.672100524516594*^9, 3.672100559554373*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3608]:=",ExpressionUUID->"658bac7b-e50f-4980-9cf4-567383fb49bf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TangentNormalVectorColor", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<TangentNormalVectorColor is a color directive that defines the \
color for the tangent normal vector of a parameterized curve on a surface in \
3D.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100451587705*^9, 3.672100493874409*^9}, {
  3.672100524516594*^9, 3.672100577291291*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3609]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a18a562d-3b0d-4808-b515-3cf307e8190c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"DirectorVectorColor", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<DirectorVectorColor is a color directive that defines the color \
for a director of a ruled parameterization.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.672100451587705*^9, 3.672100493874409*^9}, {
  3.672100524516594*^9, 3.672100577291291*^9}, {3.800534040821962*^9, 
  3.800534064076448*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[3610]:=",ExpressionUUID->"fdf5f599-1836-43ff-8fe2-f9a9e23bdce2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
