Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Flashers", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.71984844184949*^9, 3.719848443070951*^9}, {
  3.85491873960212*^9, 
  3.854918742505799*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"07586ee6-bfb3-408f-9be6-\
44dcf89d383e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.833026040748558*^9, 
  3.833026041215804*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dc0369f6-8b23-46a0-9c33-\
aff1c7850742"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5557187955369*^9, 
  3.5557187959350986`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"65e95224-87ac-4471-9717-\
cfc852db4e22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this section, we set up variables and functions that allow the design \
and visualization of flashers. A flasher design can be characterized by \
several parameters:\n\t",
 StyleBox["r",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " - is the number of rings, i.e., the number of up-and-down layers in each \
half-sector, or, equivalently, the number of segments in each radial \
diagonal.\n\t",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " - is the height order. The desired height of the folded form is ",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " panels, i.e., each ring is ",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " panels high. ",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is also the number of turns a diagonal makes going from bottom to top.\n\t",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " - is the rotational order. ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "=4 for square, 6 for hexagonal, and so forth.\n\t",
 StyleBox["n",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " - is the radial order. It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s the number of \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]natural\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] panel increments there \
are in the CP. So ",
 StyleBox["n ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "= ",
 StyleBox["r ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\[Times] ",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".\nThose are all integers. There is also one floating-point value:\n\t",
 StyleBox["dr",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " - is the radial increment. Basically, vertices at the same height in the \
folded form are spaced radially by this amount (relative to the radial \
distance of the corresponding inner polygon vertex). This is the value that \
results in the imperfect symmetry of the crease pattern; the larger the value \
of ",
 StyleBox["dr",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", the faster that outer rings grow in height and the more \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]curved\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] are the diagonal \
folds."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555715202248166*^9, 3.555715278466609*^9}, {
   3.555715315713017*^9, 3.5557153274876633`*^9}, {3.555715370925275*^9, 
   3.555715571967838*^9}, {3.555767232880168*^9, 3.555767287483068*^9}, {
   3.5558543045245733`*^9, 3.5558543047713203`*^9}, 3.555854343386554*^9, {
   3.555954017370488*^9, 
   3.555954222426693*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e1dd9a61-f36a-401b-bcf2-\
3b15ed9f9340"],

Cell["\<\
We analyze a flasher by parameterizing the vertices of its crease pattern \
(CP) and folded form (FF). We place constraints on the vertices of the folded \
form, then solve for the vertices of the CP in such a way that we enforce \
isometry between the CP and FF.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.55571558214567*^9, 
  3.555715644835424*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1b7c1ef0-5951-4d8d-86dc-\
63f1fd7d378c"],

Cell["\<\
This version is heavily rewritten from the file eyeglass_flasher_13_ma8.nb, \
modified to be compatible with (and make use of) Tessellatica 11. Many of the \
functions have been renamed and, in some cases, rewritten with different \
arguments, so this file and eyeglass_flasher_13_ma8.nb are generally \
incompatible.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555711879968774*^9, 3.555711888983967*^9}, {
  3.555853697037015*^9, 3.555853702156172*^9}, {3.719848341759891*^9, 
  3.719848415155447*^9}, {3.719857702067972*^9, 3.719857747929621*^9}, {
  3.719943164767871*^9, 
  3.7199431655905*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4eecc2e1-31f8-4e83-9c1d-33343831fd9b"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Paraboloidal flashers", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.825603350174984*^9, 3.8256033543829403`*^9}, {
  3.825670181416965*^9, 
  3.825670182918375*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ef0a33e8-6e63-4bd2-bf92-\
0ae39961d0a2"],

Cell["\<\
In Tessellation 13.0 and above, this section augments the original Flasher \
code with new functions to generate a paraboloidal flasher, and also to \
generate a cut pattern to make one from a flat shape.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8330259857191563`*^9, 3.833026015398644*^9}, {
  3.85491879169212*^9, 
  3.85491881052496*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cd3216e1-5299-4958-9bbe-\
46bc25fc9fb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tessellatica now includes routines to support the analysis of paraboloidal \
flashers. In essence, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll make the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]crease pattern\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] a 3D shape, by \
augmenting the 2D coordinates with a paraboloidal sag function that is \
parameterized on the focal length ",
 StyleBox["f",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of the paraboloid."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.825603357790751*^9, 3.825603455423814*^9}, {
  3.825670195868383*^9, 3.825670219068948*^9}, {3.825670916825803*^9, 
  3.825670918467895*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5040100c-bd84-4795-9824-\
739d4b663087"],

Cell["\<\
We\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll introduce a concept of the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Deployed Pattern\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], or DP, which \
is the 3D shape. Basically, the 3D points of the DP are the 2D points of the \
CP plus the appropriate sag value in the z-direction.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.825603470495442*^9, 
  3.825603535327972*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1f44c190-7c90-4576-8448-\
91c618c8e603"],

Cell["For a paraboloid, that sag function is:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.825603541160013*^9, 
  3.825603551303989*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7fe1e25a-0237-45d6-8033-\
b78ff7633b1b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "f"}], "}"}], ",", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox["y", "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{"4", "f"}]]}], "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.825603559219393*^9, 3.8256035820169497`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[4091]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7d3fedee-ac2e-4499-8233-5e6b5d0d4ba5"],

Cell["\<\
The concept of a Deployed Pattern is broader than just paraboloids; we can \
add a general sag function to any deployed form.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9118277794571238`*^9, 
  3.911827818387195*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"03a30df5-a63e-4245-bf03-\
21b35fcb866d"],

Cell["\<\
Any function that has DP in its name is a function that has been added to \
support 3D deployed forms.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.825670236938045*^9, 3.825670264990031*^9}, {
  3.911827828285921*^9, 
  3.9118278308460608`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bd6ff137-8e6a-4212-b170-\
bbea17311281"],

Cell["\<\
Functions that begin with ParaboloidalFlasher are specific to paraboloidal \
flashers.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.911827840988452*^9, 
  3.911827861167266*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0f70c6ec-99bf-471c-aa13-\
ca8a9f4dc474"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Utilities", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7199433247911987`*^9, 3.719943325830392*^9}, {
  3.8256036140324507`*^9, 
  3.825603619713095*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f8fffcd5-35ee-471d-9425-\
ab6bd0d5c9da"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "FlasherRotation2D[",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]\nFlasherRotation3D[",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "]"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.719848637886105*^9, 3.719848640054967*^9}, {
   3.7198487009771757`*^9, 3.719848720411163*^9}, 3.719919275742906*^9, 
   3.719943219260483*^9, {3.719943285676097*^9, 
   3.71994329931502*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0f607b14-20de-4be9-8a19-\
bab3891f382b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "FlasherRotation2D[",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] returns the 2D rotation matrix for (",
 StyleBox["k/m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ") turns about the origin."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555749799375511*^9, 3.555749831237354*^9}, {
   3.555749866066943*^9, 3.555749868658613*^9}, 3.555749909634082*^9, 
   3.719943219284566*^9, 
   3.719943285694276*^9},ExpressionUUID->"f3d5fb35-bf1b-4328-9f24-\
5d02b368c831"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FlasherRotation2D", "[", 
   RowBox[{"k_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"k", "/", "m"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", 
         RowBox[{"k", "/", "m"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"k", "/", "m"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"k", "/", "m"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555749833097237*^9, 3.555749845548101*^9}, 
   3.719943219297065*^9, 3.719943285701698*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[4092]:=",ExpressionUUID->"aae11430-fc50-496d-a162-eac39c5b43dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "FlasherRotation3D[",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] returns the 3D rotation matrix for (",
 StyleBox["k/m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ") turns about the z axis."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555749850220929*^9, 3.555749863923072*^9}, 
   3.555749911167893*^9, 
   3.7199432993326263`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"be670c4d-5299-486e-99a7-\
db6a6bd6dcb0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FlasherRotation3D", "[", 
   RowBox[{"k_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"k", "/", "m"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", 
         RowBox[{"k", "/", "m"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"k", "/", "m"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"k", "/", "m"}]}], "]"}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555749871145731*^9, 3.555749903917996*^9}, 
   3.7199432993406687`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[4093]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d657d1f2-25c5-43e2-9068-4396cc267b4a"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Vertex indexing", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7198787732809143`*^9, 
  3.719878786974567*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9e8742ba-adad-42a2-988b-\
68d78376f288"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.719918974223248*^9, 
  3.7199189746712503`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"80c04332-8985-4f2b-af10-\
b55ef1227576"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both crease pattern points and folded form points in a crease pattern of \
order ",
 StyleBox["n",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " are vectors of the form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"i", ",", "j", ",", " ", "k"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1532a339-2200-43ca-a444-35abcee78fe3"],
 " for crease pattern points, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["pp", 
    RowBox[{"i", ",", "j", ",", "k"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "df88caa6-f5cb-4de3-a028-2b5c92e50f93"],
 " for folded form points, with indices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"i", "=", "0"}], ",", "...", ",", "n", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"j", "=", "0"}], ",", "...", ",", "n", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"k", "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"0", "..."}], "m"}], "-", "1"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"3ecc35c0-25c4-41c1-b84a-e03cf2e4e1cf"],
 ", where ",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["j",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " are indices of the point position within a single sector and ",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " specifies the rotational position. Because of symmetry, we only need to \
parameterize a single sector of points."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555715723082554*^9, 3.555715849269429*^9}, {
  3.55571588994154*^9, 3.555715901298204*^9}, {3.555748626639209*^9, 
  3.555748717007893*^9}, {3.555751451057632*^9, 3.5557514520937357`*^9}, {
  3.719918993503681*^9, 3.719919003007902*^9}, {3.719945774599575*^9, 
  3.7199457888557253`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a4d51ee0-d370-4f25-a028-\
64771959f4f5"],

