Cell["\<\
There are two ways to triangulate each quad, of course, so there are many \
ways to create the diagonals (and the different ways set which direction each \
panel flexes in the folded form and/or during deployment). We give a few \
possible algorithms.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.719850789302285*^9, {3.719850845632565*^9, 3.719850851162705*^9}, {
   3.719943859286971*^9, 
   3.719943888070436*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1f48bf45-b244-4523-9490-\
0504dc5872d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "FlasherSectorDiagFoldLinesX[",
 StyleBox["v",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["r",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["k",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] returns a list of the diagonal folds that cross each quad."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555798834675611*^9, 3.555798970778313*^9}, {
   3.5557994867296677`*^9, 3.555799530933684*^9}, {3.555804606163015*^9, 
   3.555804626337354*^9}, 3.555854308427391*^9, 3.555854346149694*^9, {
