}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Planar flasher construction", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555839231821539*^9, 3.555839232787725*^9}, {
  3.555952624316916*^9, 3.555952627690748*^9}, {3.719931002693582*^9, 
  3.7199310034598083`*^9}, {3.719936385766007*^9, 3.71993638772436*^9}, {
  3.825679514808774*^9, 
  3.825679518392346*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dd352279-342c-48cf-9692-\
9ad2b7d5692d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.719931102291793*^9, 
  3.719931102883951*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"92e6d9e9-41c1-4fb2-b781-\
c6ed5ae2f663"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here we set up a solution that solves all the relevant equations for \
ordinary (planar-CP) flashers. You can play with these values to change the \
design:\n\t",
 StyleBox["r",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the number of rings.\n\t",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the height order (how many turns a diagonal takes to get from \
the bottom to the top of a ring)\n\t",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the rotational symmetry\n\t",
 StyleBox["dr",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the radial spacing of successive vertices in the same plane.\n\
Note that the bottom is not necessarily perfectly flat in the folded form. \
Rather, the bottom of the outer ring and the central polygon are both forced \
to ",
 StyleBox["z",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "=0, but the other \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]down\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
vertices can (and typically do) take on slightly nonzero values."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555839241395936*^9, 3.555839263945986*^9}, {
   3.5558406922764997`*^9, 3.555840696315197*^9}, {3.555850898870534*^9, 
   3.555850902915904*^9}, {3.555850936122521*^9, 3.555851037539441*^9}, {
   3.555853630666301*^9, 3.5558536429924*^9}, 3.55585432144669*^9, 
   3.555854357880516*^9, {3.555952632059319*^9, 3.55595263972264*^9}, {
   3.555953463903367*^9, 3.5559535181282387`*^9}, {3.71994562255157*^9, 
   3.719945639647678*^9}, {3.825607516811368*^9, 3.825607552924202*^9}, 
   3.825611404095207*^9, {3.825679523328209*^9, 
   3.82567954067247*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6ef16e5a-d99f-4bbb-bac4-\
742746892082"],

Cell["\<\
If the root-finder fails, the isometry values will be reported. Any values \
that are not zero (or nearly so) represent an isometry violation between the \
crease pattern and folded form.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.555851718871272*^9, 3.555851767067861*^9}, 
   3.719931106622401*^9},ExpressionUUID->"dcd4ae2b-3fca-4b5e-a478-\
7a51173fbd32"]
}, Closed]],

