   3.703681108802248*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"645e5703-6428-43df-a8c5-\
a8c4dcba0f55"],

Cell["\<\
required to attain a 180\[Degree] fold or, if FoldAngles is specified, each \
given fold angle, and\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.62791156625606*^9},ExpressionUUID->"2f8ed970-da49-419d-aa7f-0e4b2ec908f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Output line styles are still symbolic. You should use \
ScoringStyle[ScoreLineThickness\[Rule]",
 StyleBox["hairline",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "] to render the style appropriate for the laser cutter (",
 StyleBox["hairline",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " = 0.216 for CorelDraw and the TopWisdom driver)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.626458599844168*^9},ExpressionUUID->"bd717907-afc2-4cbb-bb5d-\
8add12750315"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The FoldAngles option extends the interpretation of angles to allow for \
extra-wide kerfs, e.g., for layers that wrap around other layers:\n\tFor \
angles in the range [0,\[Dash]\[Pi]] (ordinary mountain), the kerf width is \
0;\n\tFor angles in the range [0,+\[Pi]] (ordinary valley), the kerf width is \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"w", "=", 
    RowBox[{"2", "t", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"075eb8fd-134a-4637-9bf7-f05ab685f621"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "382c3c8f-9e1b-4ce7-aa84-7fe6e7283506"],
 " is the veneer thickness.\n\tFor larger positive angles, the kerf width is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", "t", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "/", "\[Pi]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2f5711f4-3cb3-479c-bb35-d8f116e75cef"],
 ", so that each incremental value of \[Pi] adds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", "t"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "79031adb-5828-4784-9e46-2bf41ce1b84a"],
 " to the kerf width.\n\tFor larger negative angles, the kerf width is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", "t", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"|", "\[Gamma]", "|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"/", "\[Pi]"}], "-", "1"}]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"497e3254-9e63-4c55-86a1-8db6852f7d68"],
 ", again so that each incremental value of \[Pi] adds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", "t"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "54911491-96e9-4837-b5d5-ffdb6ab672c9"],
 " to the kerf width.\nThe reason for this behavior is to provide a way to \
create extra-large kerfs for folds that must wrap around multiple layers."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.703680586756813*^9, 3.7036808105024033`*^9}, {
  3.703680848974574*^9, 3.703681078217067*^9}, {3.703681583023155*^9, 
  3.703681599757542*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e2e5b8c8-a082-4408-a4ef-\
0e2bc265219f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"VeneerThickness", "::", "usage"}], 
   "=", "\"\<VeneerThickness is an option to VeneerScoringGraphics that \
specifies the thickness of the material, which, in turn, is used to determine \
the widths of the kerfs for the valley folds.\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.624891292191949*^9, 3.624891348379841*^9}, 
   3.624913968548517*^9, {3.624915103387578*^9, 3.624915103827613*^9}, 
